#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:86
#, markdown-text
msgid "![The results of a shooter with a wreath card](../images/screenshots/results.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:88
#, markdown-text
msgid "The programme is now *completed* with *Total 374 / 400*. Below it you see *Award: Wreath card*: 374 points reach the 360 an Elite shooter needs, so Standblatt gave her the card. At the top you see *All programmes have results.*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:90
#, markdown-text
msgid "Close the results. Lena has moved to **Completed** with the badge *awards to hand out*, and lane 3 is *free* again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:91
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "9. Register a second shooter"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:94
#, markdown-text
msgid "Marco is not in the shooter list yet, so you create him at the desk."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:100
#, markdown-text
msgid "Click **New shooter** next to the search field."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:100
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Club**: *SG Hilltown* (the list suggests it now). **First name**: *Marco*, **Last name**: *Brunner*, **Birthday**: 3 March 1975."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:100
#, markdown-text
msgid "Click **Create and register**. The registration opens: Marco is *Senior*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:100
#, markdown-text
msgid "Click lane **4**, tick **Championship** and click **Register**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:100
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under **Shooting**, click **Results** next to Marco, type *88*, *90*, *89* and *85* and press **Enter**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:102
#, markdown-text
msgid "Marco's total is 352. You see *No award reached.*: a Senior needs 355 for the wreath card."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:103
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "10. See the ranking"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:106
#, markdown-text
msgid "Click **Rankings** in the sidebar."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:108
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Rankings of an event with more shooters](../images/screenshots/rankings.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:110
#, markdown-text
msgid "You see the table *Championship* with *40 shots · 2 shooters*: Lena on rank 1 with 374, Marco on rank 2 with 352, each with the four series and the total. The ranking updates by itself whenever a result is saved, on every computer that shows it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:111
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:59
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What you have done"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:114
#, markdown-text
msgid "You have set up a range, created an event with a programme, prices and an award, registered two shooters on lanes, entered their results and seen the live ranking. That is the work of a shooting day."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:115
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:63
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:119
#, markdown-text
msgid "Show the ranking on a screen in the hall: [Kiosk screens](../how-to/kiosk.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:119
#, markdown-text
msgid "Print lane sheets, wreath cards and results at the range: [Connect a printer](../how-to/connect-printer.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:119
#, markdown-text
msgid "When the event is over and the ranking is checked, close it: [Closing an event](../explanation/closing.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/annual-programme.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Run an annual programme over the season"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/annual-programme.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "You need this when members shoot a programme as often as they like over the season and a club championship ranks the best three results of each shooter. It needs the permission *Configure events* (see [Roles](../user-guide/users.md#roles)); entering the results needs *Run events*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/annual-programme.md:5
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/feldschiessen.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Create the event {#event}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/annual-programme.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under **Events**, click **New event** and choose **Annual programme or training**. It switches on the modules *Attempts* and *Classifications*; choose **Club championship** instead if the ranking should also run on a kiosk display."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/annual-programme.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "Enter the **Name**, e.g. *Annual programme 2027*, and as **Date** the first day of the season. Its year sets the age categories."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/annual-programme.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "Tick the range under **Ranges**, or none if the results come on paper only (see [Events without lanes](../user-guide/events.md#no-lanes))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/annual-programme.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "Switch on **Period (season)**, enter the **First day** and the **Last day**, and under **Shooting times** tick the weekdays of the club's training with their times. No weekday ticked means every day of the period."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/annual-programme.md:13
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Add the programme {#programme}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/annual-programme.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open **Configuration** → **Programmes** and click **New programme** (or **Add from …** to take it from the library, a file or an earlier event)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/annual-programme.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "Enter the name and the series."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/annual-programme.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under **Attempts**, tick **Unlimited** and set **Counting attempt** to **The best**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/annual-programme.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under **Prices (CHF)**, tick every age category that may shoot and enter the price. The second field is the price of every further attempt: empty means the same price, 0 means the programme is paid once."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/annual-programme.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Rank the best three attempts {#classification}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/annual-programme.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open **Configuration** → **Classifications** and click **New classification**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/annual-programme.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "Enter a **Name**, e.g. *Club championship*, choose the annual programme as **Programme 1** and set **Counting attempts** to 3."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/annual-programme.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "Switch on **Rank only shooters with all counting results** if only shooters with three results should get a rank; the others are then listed below the ranking."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/annual-programme.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "Add **Classes** if juniors and adults are ranked apart, e.g. *Juniors* with U17 to U21 and *Elite* with the others."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/annual-programme.md:30
#, markdown-text
msgid "All settings of the editor are described in [Classifications](../user-guide/classifications.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/annual-programme.md:31
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Enter the results during the season {#results}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/annual-programme.md:36
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/import-results.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open the event and click **Enter results** in the sidebar."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/annual-programme.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "Choose the **Programme**, type a licence number or a name into **Shooter** and press ++enter++."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/annual-programme.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "Type the series and press ++enter++. Every result of a shooter is a new attempt."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/annual-programme.md:38
#, markdown-text
msgid "Results from the scoring system can also be imported as a file (see [Import results from the scoring system](import-results.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/annual-programme.md:40
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Rankings** shows the programme with the best attempt of each shooter (*2/5*: the second of five attempts counts) and the club championship with the sum of the best three.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/annual-programme.md:41
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "End the season {#close}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/annual-programme.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid "When the last results are in and checked, open **Configuration** → **Copy & close** and click **Close event**. What closing changes is explained in [Closing an event](../explanation/closing.md); next season starts with [Take over last year's event](next-year.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/army-sheet.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Print results onto the army's lane sheets"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/army-sheet.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "You need this when the shooters' results must end up on pre-printed sheets, e.g. the lane sheets the army supplies for the obligatory programme, and you would rather print them than fill them in by hand. It needs the permissions *Print forms*, *Configure events* and *Ranges and printers* (see [Roles](../user-guide/users.md#roles))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/army-sheet.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "Before you start, scan an empty sheet as PNG or JPEG and keep a few spare sheets for test prints."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/army-sheet.md:7
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "1. Prepare the programme {#programme}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/army-sheet.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "Check that **Club modules** in the club part of the sidebar has *Print forms* switched on (it is on unless someone switched it off)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/army-sheet.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under **Configuration** → **Programmes** of the event, open the programme and tick **Single shots** for every series whose shots the sheet has boxes for. Do this before the first registration: once shooters are registered, the series are fixed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/army-sheet.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Save** the programme."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/army-sheet.md:13
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2. Create the form {#form}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/army-sheet.md:22
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/certificates.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open **Print forms** in the club part of the sidebar and click **New print form**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/army-sheet.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid "Enter a name (e.g. *Obligatory programme 300 m*), choose **Prints** *Results of a programme* and the paper size closest to the sheet, then **Create**. The editor opens."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/army-sheet.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid "In **Form** on the right, set **Width (mm)** and **Height (mm)** to the size of the sheet, then **Upload a scan** under **Scan of the empty form**. The scan shows behind the sheet while editing; it is never printed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/army-sheet.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid "From **Fields** on the left, drag the shooter's fields (e.g. **Last name**, **First name**, **Year of birth**, **License number**) onto their boxes on the scan."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/army-sheet.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid "From the group **Single shots**, drag **Shots of series 1** onto the first shot box of that series. It is a row of boxes, 8 mm apart; drag the pink dot on its last box until every value sits in its box, or set **dx (mm)** under **Properties**. Repeat for the other series."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/army-sheet.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid "From **Result**, add the series totals (**Series 1** …) and the **Total** where the sheet has boxes for them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '7. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/army-sheet.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Save**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/army-sheet.md:24
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Print forms](../images/screenshots/print-forms.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/army-sheet.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "How to move, align and snap elements is in [Print forms](../user-guide/print-forms.md#arrange), every field in [Form placeholders](../reference/form-placeholders.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/army-sheet.md:27
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "3. Calibrate the printer {#calibrate}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/army-sheet.md:33
#, markdown-text
msgid "Put an empty sheet into the printer at the range."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/army-sheet.md:33
#, markdown-text
msgid "Click **Test print**: the saved form opens as PDF with made-up values and without the scan. Print it at actual size (no fit to page)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/army-sheet.md:33
#, markdown-text
msgid "Measure how far the values are off their boxes and enter it as **Printer offset right (mm)** and **Printer offset down (mm)** under **Form** (negative to move left or up)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/army-sheet.md:33
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Save** and repeat from step 1 until the values sit in the boxes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/army-sheet.md:34
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "4. Assign the form and the printer {#assign}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/army-sheet.md:38
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under **Configuration** → **Programmes** of the event, open the programme and choose the form in the section **Print form**. It is saved at once; this works while shooters are registered."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/army-sheet.md:38
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under **Ranges → Set up the printers** of the range, choose the printer for **Print forms (pre-printed)**, e.g. with its manual feed as tray, and **Save** (see [Connect a printer](connect-printer.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/army-sheet.md:39
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "5. Print the sheets {#print}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/army-sheet.md:41
#, markdown-text
msgid "Once all series of the programme are in, its results show **Print onto form**: in the results at the desk and on scorer links at the lane (see [Helpers](../user-guide/helpers.md)). On **Enter results**, every line under *Entered now* has its own print button. Put a sheet into the printer and click it. Without an online print agent, the PDF opens and is printed from the browser."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/certificates.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Print certificates for the best ranks"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/certificates.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "You need this when the winners of a programme or a classification get a certificate with their name and rank, e.g. ranks 1 to 3 at the prize giving. Creating the form needs the permission *Print forms*, printing *Run events* (see [Roles](../user-guide/users.md#roles))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/certificates.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "1. Create the certificate form {#form}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/certificates.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "Enter a name (e.g. *Certificate*), choose **Prints** *A rank* and a paper size such as *A4 portrait (210 × 297 mm)*, then **Create**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/certificates.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "From **Fields**, add what the certificate shows: **Name** from *Shooter*, **Rank**, **Ranking** and **Class** from *Rank*, **Total** from *Result*, and **Own text** for fixed words such as *Certificate*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/certificates.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "For a logo, **Upload image** in the image library below the list of **Print forms** first; it then appears in the group **Images** of the fields (see [Images](../user-guide/print-forms.md#images))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/certificates.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Save**, then check the result with **PDF preview**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/certificates.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "On paper with a pre-printed design, add a scan of it under **Scan of the empty form** and calibrate the printer as for the [army's lane sheets](army-sheet.md#calibrate)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/certificates.md:15
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2. Choose the printer {#printer}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/certificates.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under **Ranges → Set up the printers** of the event's first range, choose the printer for **Certificates** and **Save** (see [Connect a printer](connect-printer.md)). Without it, the certificates open as one PDF."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/certificates.md:19
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "3. Print the certificates {#print}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/certificates.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open **Rankings** of the event."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/certificates.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid "Click **Certificates** in the header of the programme or classification. The button appears once the club has a form that prints a rank."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/certificates.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid "Choose the **Print form**, for a classification with several classes the **Class**, and the ranks with **From rank** and **To rank** (1 to 3 unless changed)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/certificates.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid "Click **Print certificates**, or **PDF** to open them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/certificates.md:27
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:47
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Certificates from a ranking](../images/screenshots/certificates.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/certificates.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "One page prints per ranked shooter. A programme's certificate knows the shooter's results too, e.g. the series."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/connect-printer.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Connect a printer at the range"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/connect-printer.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "You need this when lane sheets, control strips and wreath cards should come out of the printer at the range instead of opening as PDF. It needs the permission *Ranges and printers* (see [Roles](../user-guide/users.md#roles))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/connect-printer.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "A computer next to the printers runs the print agent: a Windows PC or a Mac with the Standblatt Print Agent app, or a Linux computer such as a Raspberry Pi with the headless agent. Why it works this way is in [Printing](../explanation/printing.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/connect-printer.md:7
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "With the app on Windows or a Mac {#app}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/connect-printer.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "Download it from the [latest release](https://github.com/standblatt/print-agent/releases/latest): `Standblatt-Print-Agent-Setup.exe` for Windows, `standblatt-print-agent-app-darwin-arm64.dmg` for a Mac with Apple silicon (`-amd64.dmg` for an Intel Mac), the `.deb` or `.rpm` for Linux."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/connect-printer.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "Install it. The app is not signed yet: Windows asks once, **More info → Run anyway**; on a Mac drag it into *Applications* and open it the first time with a right click → **Open**. On Windows it installs for the current user without admin rights, with a shortcut in the start menu and on the desktop, and starts with Windows."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/connect-printer.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "In the app, click **Connect a range**. It shows a code such as `K7QD-4MZP` and opens **Connect a print agent** in the browser."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/connect-printer.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "Log in if asked, check the computer named on the page, choose the **Club**, the **Range** and the agent's **Name**, and **Connect**. The code is valid for ten minutes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/connect-printer.md:15
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:38
#, markdown-text
msgid "![A code in the app](../images/app/print-agent-code.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/connect-printer.md:17
#, markdown-text
msgid "If the browser on that computer is not at hand, open **Ranges → Set up the printers** of the range on any other computer, type the code into the field next to **Connect by code** and click it: the computer is connected to that range under its own name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/connect-printer.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "For a second range on the same computer, e.g. *Pistol 25 m* and *Pistol 50 m*, click **Connect another range** in the app and repeat steps 3 and 4."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/connect-printer.md:20
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "With the headless agent on Linux {#headless}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/connect-printer.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open **Ranges** and click **Set up the printers** of the range."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/connect-printer.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under **Print agents**, enter a name (e.g. *Pi hall 1*) and click **Add print agent**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/connect-printer.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "Click **Copy** to copy the two lines `STANDBLATT_URL` and `STANDBLATT_AGENT_TOKEN`. The token is shown only now."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/connect-printer.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "Install and start the agent with these settings as described in the [README of the print agent](https://github.com/standblatt/print-agent#readme)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/connect-printer.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "For a second range on the same computer, add an agent there too and give the agent both tokens, separated by a comma."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/connect-printer.md:29
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Choose the printers {#printers}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/connect-printer.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open **Ranges → Set up the printers** of the range. The agent shows *online* with its version and operating system; its printers appear once it has connected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/connect-printer.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "For each document, choose the printer, then its options (tray, paper, two-sided …, as the agent reports them for that printer; on Linux further `lp` options such as `fit-to-page` go in the text field)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/connect-printer.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "Click **Test page** in the row: a small page (90 × 29 mm) with club, range, printer, options and the time prints with the options of that row. A label printer prints it as a label, other printers in the top-left corner of the sheet."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/connect-printer.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "Click **Save** in the row. A document left on *browser (PDF)* keeps opening as PDF."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/connect-printer.md:37
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Printing](../images/screenshots/printing.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/connect-printer.md:39
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Certificates* are the certificates from the rankings, *Print forms (pre-printed)* every other [print form](../user-guide/print-forms.md) of the club. Rankings are never sent to a printer.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/connect-printer.md:40
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Check that it prints {#jobs}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/connect-printer.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid "Print something, e.g. a lane sheet at the next registration, and look at **Recent jobs** on the same page: *done* means it printed, *failed* shows the error next to it. A job that the agent does not confirm within two minutes is retried; after three attempts it fails."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/connect-printer.md:44
#, markdown-text
msgid "To give up a computer, click **revoke** next to its agent; with the app, also remove the range under **Advanced** and uninstall the app. All screens of the printing page are described in [Printing](../user-guide/printing.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/feldschiessen.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Set up a Feldschiessen over a period"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/feldschiessen.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "You need this when the Feldschiessen is shot over weeks, e.g. from the opening of the range until 31 August plus the official weekend, and the results come from the desk, from scorers at the lane or on paper. It needs the permission *Configure events* (see [Roles](../user-guide/users.md#roles))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/feldschiessen.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under **Events**, click **New event** and choose **Feldschiessen**. It switches on lane assignment, awards, the club competition, kiosk displays and helper links."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/feldschiessen.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "Enter the **Name** and as **Date** the main day, e.g. the Saturday of the official weekend. Its year sets the age categories."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/feldschiessen.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "Tick the ranges under **Ranges**, e.g. *Rifle 300 m* and *Pistol 25 m*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/feldschiessen.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under **Shooting days**, add the days of the official weekend with their shooting times."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/feldschiessen.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "Switch on **Period (season)**, enter the **First day** and the **Last day**, and under **Shooting times** tick the weekdays the range is open, with their times. The single days of step 4 add to the period or replace its times on that date."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/feldschiessen.md:14
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Add the programmes {#programmes}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/feldschiessen.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open **Configuration** → **Programmes** and add the programmes, from the editor or with **Add from …** (library, programme file or last year's event). One programme per distance; weapons with their own award limits, e.g. *Stgw 90* and *Stgw 57*, are variants of the same name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/feldschiessen.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under **Prices (CHF)**, tick every age category that may shoot. For a free Feldschiessen, enter 0."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/feldschiessen.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under **Awards**, click **Add award** for each award, with its **Kind** and the minimum total per age category."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/feldschiessen.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "Click **Create**. On an event with several ranges, then choose the **Range** of the programme under **Use**; it is saved at once."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/feldschiessen.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Choose how the results come in {#results}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/feldschiessen.md:24
#, markdown-text
msgid "The ways can be mixed within one event."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/feldschiessen.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "**At the desk:** keep the module *Lane assignment*. Register each shooter on a lane from the [Dashboard](../user-guide/dashboard.md) and enter the series under **Results** when the targets come back (see [Results](../user-guide/results.md)). Switch on *Lane sheet* and *Control strip* under **Modules** if they should print at registration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/feldschiessen.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "**At the lane:** create a scorer link for each group of lanes under **Helper links** in the configuration (see [Helpers](../user-guide/helpers.md#create)); the scorers enter the series on a phone or tablet."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/feldschiessen.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "**On paper:** switch off *Lane assignment* under **Modules** if nobody is registered on a lane. Type the sheets in on **Enter results** (see [Enter results](../user-guide/results-entry.md#quick)), or import the file of the scoring system (see [Import results from the scoring system](import-results.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/feldschiessen.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid "Switch off what the Feldschiessen does not use, e.g. *Kiosk displays* or *Club competition*, under **Configuration** → **Modules**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/hand-out-awards.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Hand out awards and cash prizes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/hand-out-awards.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "You need this when shooters collect their wreath cards, prizes in kind and cash prizes at the desk and you want to know who still has something to collect. It needs the module *Awards* and the permission *Run events*, or a helper link of the results clerk."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/hand-out-awards.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Hand out to a shooter {#handout}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/hand-out-awards.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "On the **Dashboard**, find the shooter in the *Completed* list and click the *awards to hand out* badge. The results open with the awards of every programme."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/hand-out-awards.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "Hand out what is listed: wreath cards, prizes in kind and cash."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/hand-out-awards.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "Click **Awards handed out**. The registration now carries the time of the handout and a green *awards handed out* badge."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/hand-out-awards.md:12
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Dashboard](../images/screenshots/dashboard.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/hand-out-awards.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "A shooter not in sight on the dashboard is found with ++f4++ and the search, or by scanning the code on the lane sheet (see [Dashboard](../user-guide/dashboard.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/hand-out-awards.md:15
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Take a wrong click back {#undo}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/hand-out-awards.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "Click the green *awards handed out* badge on the dashboard, or **Take back** in the results, and confirm. The awards count as open again. Only club members can take a handout back, not helper links."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/hand-out-awards.md:19
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "See what is still open {#open}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/hand-out-awards.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under **Statistics**, download the report **Awards to hand out** as PDF or CSV. It lists every award not yet collected with shooter, club, programme, kind and value, the number of shooters with awards to collect and the cash still to pay out."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/hand-out-awards.md:23
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Let a helper hand out {#helper}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/hand-out-awards.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid "For a separate award desk without a club account, create a helper link with the role **Results clerk** (see [Helpers](../user-guide/helpers.md#create)). It sees the completed list and marks awards as handed out like the dashboard."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/import-results.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Import results from the scoring system"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/import-results.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "You need this when the results of many shooters are in a file, e.g. exported from the electronic scoring system or typed into a spreadsheet. It needs the permission *Configure events* (see [Roles](../user-guide/users.md#roles)); the event must not be closed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/import-results.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare the file {#file}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/import-results.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "Export or save the results as CSV with a header row and one line per shooter and programme. The columns are listed under [CSV import](../reference/csv-import.md#results): at least `license` (or `firstname` and `lastname`), `programme` and the series `s1`, `s2`, …."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/import-results.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "In the `programme` column, use the programme's barcode or its name, with the variant in parentheses where there are variants, e.g. `Championship (Sport)`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/import-results.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "If the file has a `club` column, check that every club is in the club list under **Master data** → **Clubs**; add missing ones there."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/import-results.md:11
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Import it {#import}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/import-results.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "Click **Import CSV**, choose the file and click **Import**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/import-results.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "*Imported: … results, … new shooters.* means you are done; the results are on **Rankings**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/import-results.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "Import a file only once. A second import is refused for programmes that are shot once (the shooters already have results), but a programme with several [attempts](../user-guide/programmes.md#attempts) takes every line again as a further attempt."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/import-results.md:19
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Fix line errors {#errors}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/import-results.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid "With any error, nothing is imported and the dialog shows *Nothing imported, please fix these lines:* with the line numbers. Fix every listed line in the file and import the whole file again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/import-results.md:35
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Message | Fix |\n|---|---|\n| Programme \"…\" not found | write the programme as on its programme page, with the variant if there are several, or use its barcode |\n| Club \"…\" is not in the club list | correct the spelling or add the club under **Clubs** |\n| No shooter with the licence …; add first and last name to create one | add `firstname` and `lastname` to the line, so the shooter can be created |\n| Several shooters are called …; add the birthday or the licence | add `birthday` or `license` to the line |\n| Series … is missing, … is not a number | fill in every series of the programme; decimals take `.` or `,` |\n| Series …: points must be between 0 and … | correct the points; the maximum is set by the programme's series |\n| Series …: enter all … shots | give every single shot of the series, or none and only the series total |\n| The shooter already has results in … | remove the line; the results are in Standblatt already |\n| The same shooter and programme appear twice in the file | keep one of the two lines |\n| The shooter has no attempts left in … | remove the line, or raise the attempts of the programme |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/import-results.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "A message about the header row (*The header row needs the column programme*, *… the column license or the columns firstname and lastname*) means a column name is missing or misspelt in the first line."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/import-results.md:38
#, markdown-text
msgid "Shooters who are not in the master data are created by the import. Single results can still be corrected afterwards in the results of the registration (see [Results](../user-guide/results.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/kiosk.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Show the rankings on a screen in the hall"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/kiosk.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "You need this when shooters and spectators should follow the live rankings on a screen at the range. The screen needs a browser and internet, no login. Setting it up needs the permission *Configure events* (see [Roles](../user-guide/users.md#roles))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/kiosk.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under **Configuration** → **Modules** of the event, switch on *Kiosk displays*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/kiosk.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open **Kiosk displays** in the configuration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/kiosk.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "Enter a name for the screen (e.g. *Hall 1*), choose **Dark** or **Light** and, if the screen should not use the event's language, a language. On an event with several ranges, choose the range the screen shows, or *All ranges*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/kiosk.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "Click **Create kiosk link** and **copy** the link. It is shown only once."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/kiosk.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open the link in a browser on the screen and click the **Fullscreen** button at the top right."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/kiosk.md:12
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Kiosk screen](../images/screenshots/kiosk.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/kiosk.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "The screen updates live and reconnects by itself after a network interruption."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/kiosk.md:15
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Choose what the screen shows {#content}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/kiosk.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "A programme shows only while **Show on kiosk displays** is on on its programme page (it is on for new programmes). Staff pages, PDF and CSV rank it anyway."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/kiosk.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "A classification shows with **Show on kiosk displays** in its editor (see [Classifications](../user-guide/classifications.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/kiosk.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "With lane assignment, **Show lane status on the rankings** on **Kiosk displays** adds the lane status above the rankings."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/kiosk.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Stop a screen {#revoke}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/kiosk.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid "Click **revoke** next to the screen in the list on **Kiosk displays**: the link stops working immediately. *last seen* tells when a screen last fetched data. The parts of the link are listed in [Links](../reference/links.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/next-year.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Take over last year's event"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/next-year.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "You need this when an event comes back, e.g. next year's championship or the Feldschiessen of the next season, and should start with last year's settings and programmes instead of an empty event. It needs the permission *Configure events* (see [Roles](../user-guide/users.md#roles))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/next-year.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "Copy last year's event when the event comes back as it was. Save a template when the club runs the same kind of event several times or in different forms, e.g. an annual programme for air pistol and one for air rifle."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/next-year.md:7
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Copy last year's event {#copy}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/next-year.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under **Events**, open last year's event (closed events are under *Closed*)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/next-year.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open **Configuration** → **Copy & close** and click **Copy** next to *Copy for next year*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/next-year.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "Check the **Name** (the year and a leading number like *42.* are counted up) and the **Date** (the same date one year later). The other shooting days and the period move by as many days as the date, so choose the date on the right weekday, e.g. the Saturday of the official weekend."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/next-year.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "Click **Create copy**. The copy opens in its configuration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/next-year.md:14
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Start from a template of the club {#template}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/next-year.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open the event that is set up well and go to **Configuration** → **Copy & close**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/next-year.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "Click **Save as template**, check the **Name** (it is suggested without the year) and click **Save template**. The template is listed under *Templates* below the events."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/next-year.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "Next time, click **New event** under **Events**, choose the template below the kinds of events, enter **Name** and **Date** and click **Create**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/next-year.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "A template can be changed like an event, but it takes no registrations. **Delete** on its **Copy & close** removes it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/next-year.md:22
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Check the new event {#check}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/next-year.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid "The copy takes over the ranges, organizer, language, settings, modules, programmes with prices, awards, combinations and special prizes, and the classifications. Registrations, results, kiosk links and helper links are not copied. Before the first registration, check:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/next-year.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "**General**: the shooting days, the period and the shooting times."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/next-year.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Programmes**: prices, award tiers and limits, and which programmes are active. Changes are easiest now, before shooters are registered."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/next-year.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Modules**: what this year's event needs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/next-year.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Kiosk displays** and **Helper links**: create new links and send them out."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/next-year.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Reservations**: switch the [online booking](../user-guide/online-booking.md) on again; the copy takes over its hours, but not the link and not the deadline. Reservations belong to the range and are not copied."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/next-year.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid "What exactly is copied is listed in [Events](../user-guide/events.md#copy)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/section-championship.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Rank a section championship over several programmes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/section-championship.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "You need this when the ranking adds up several programmes of one event, e.g. a section championship as the sum of *Obligatory*, *Field match* and *Section stich*. All programmes must belong to the same event. It needs the permission *Configure events* (see [Roles](../user-guide/users.md#roles))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/section-championship.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open the event and go to **Configuration** → **Modules**. Switch on **Classifications** unless the event's kind already did."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/section-championship.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under **Programmes**, make sure every programme of the championship exists (see [Programmes](../user-guide/programmes.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/section-championship.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open **Classifications** in the configuration and click **New classification**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/section-championship.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "Enter the **Name**, e.g. *Section championship*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/section-championship.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "Choose the first programme as **Programme 1**, then **Add programme** for each further one. Leave **Counting attempts** at 1 for every programme."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/section-championship.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "Switch on **Rank only shooters with all counting results**. Shooters who are still missing a programme are listed below the ranking without a rank."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '7. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/section-championship.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "Leave **Count only the best programmes** at 0, so that every programme counts. For *the best two of three*, enter 2."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '8. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/section-championship.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "Check the **Tie-break**: the default is the SSV order; the arrows change the order of the criteria."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '9. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/section-championship.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "Add **Classes** if the championship ranks age groups apart, e.g. *Juniors* with U17 to U21 and *Elite* with the others. Without classes, everybody is in one ranking."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '10. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/section-championship.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "Switch on **Show on kiosk displays** if the ranking should run in the hall (only with the module *Kiosk displays*)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/section-championship.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "The results are entered as usual for each programme. **Rankings** shows the championship after the programme rankings, one table per class; its **PDF** and **CSV** are the report *Classifications*, and **Certificates** prints certificates for the best ranks onto a [print form](../user-guide/print-forms.md#certificates)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/section-championship.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "How totals and ties are decided is explained in [Rankings](../explanation/rankings.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/two-factor.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Protect your login with a second factor"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/two-factor.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "You need this when a password alone is not enough for your account, e.g. as a club admin. After the password, Standblatt then asks for the six-digit code of an authenticator app (Google Authenticator, Aegis, 1Password and the like)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/two-factor.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Switch it on {#on}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/two-factor.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "Install an authenticator app on your phone."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/two-factor.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open **Account** (in the user menu at the bottom of the sidebar, on the start page or in My training's sidebar)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/two-factor.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under **Second factor**, click **Set up**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/two-factor.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "Scan the QR code with the app. If it cannot scan, type the key shown below the code into the app."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/two-factor.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "Enter the code the app shows in **Code from the app** and click **Switch on**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/two-factor.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "From now on, the login asks for **Code from your authenticator app** after the password. Each code works once."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/two-factor.md:16
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:33
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Account](../images/screenshots/account.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/two-factor.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "If **Second factor** is missing on the page, the operator has switched the feature off for the whole server."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/two-factor.md:19
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Switch it off {#off}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/two-factor.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open **Account**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/two-factor.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under **Second factor**, click **Switch off**, enter your password and confirm with **Switch off**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/two-factor.md:24
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Lost the phone {#lost}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/how-to/two-factor.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "Without the app you cannot log in. Ask the platform operator to reset the second factor in the admin panel (**Reset second factor** on your user), then log in with the password and set it up again on the new phone."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/index.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Standblatt"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/index.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "Standblatt runs shooting competitions at the range: registration, lane assignment, result entry, awards, live rankings and the paperwork afterwards. It follows the rules of the Swiss Shooting Sport Federation (SSV/FST) and is used by clubs for events like an air pistol championship."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/index.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "With [My training](my-training/index.md) every shooter also gets a personal shooting diary on the phone: log a session in seconds, see the trend, the best series and where the group sits."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/index.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "![The event dashboard](images/screenshots/dashboard.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/index.md:9
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What it does"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/index.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Registration at the desk**: find a shooter by name, license number or a scanned code, pick a lane and the programmes, print the lane sheet and the control strip."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/index.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Results**: enter the series, the totals and awards follow the programme's rules; combined programmes take their series from another programme."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/index.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Live rankings**: ranked by the SSV rules, on the staff pages and on kiosk screens in the hall, updated the moment a result is saved."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/index.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Documents**: lane sheets, control strips, result sheets, wreath cards and rankings as PDF, printed at the range through a small print agent."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/index.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Reports**: statistics, club competition, revenue, awards, special prizes, all as PDF and CSV."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/index.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "**My training**: a personal training log with fast capture, hits on the target, progress and goals; competition results from Standblatt events are added with one tap."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/index.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Every club for itself**: each club keeps its own shooters, ranges, events and users. The interface is available in English, German, French and Italian."
msgstr ""

