#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Account"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "Every Standblatt user has My training: club users open it from the start page or the user menu, shooters without a club sign up themselves. Email address, password, language, second factor and deleting the account live on the [Account](../user-guide/login-language.md#account) page, which **Account** in the sidebar or **Settings → Account** opens."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Sign up"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open **Create an account** on the login page. You need your first and last name, your email address and a password of at least 10 characters. You are logged in right away."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Sign-up](../images/screenshots/my-signup.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "Standblatt sends you a link to confirm your email address. Until you confirm it, a note on the Today page reminds you; **Send again** sends a new link. The link is valid for seven days."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "Forgot your password? See [Forgotten password](../user-guide/login-language.md#password). Logged in, you change the password under [Account](../user-guide/login-language.md#account)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "Accounts created by a club admin log in with their user name instead of an email; they can add an email address on the [Account](../user-guide/login-language.md#account) page under **Login**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:17
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Profile and competition results {#competitions}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under **Settings → Profile** you can enter your **birthday** and **license number**. With both, Standblatt finds your results from events run with Standblatt by any club, for example the club championship. They show up in the **Log** under *Your competition results* once the club has closed the event, that is, once the ranking is final. Each result carries your **rank** in the programme (for example *Rank 12 of 87*). Choose the discipline and tap **Add**, or **Add all**. Added results become competition sessions with their series and keep the rank."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid "Why only closed events and how the match works: [The link to My training](../explanation/closing.md#my-training)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:23
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Own disciplines"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "Six disciplines are built in: air pistol and air rifle 10 m, pistol 25 m and 50 m, rifle 50 m and 300 m. For anything else, e.g. a field programme, add **Own discipline** in the settings with:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:30
#, markdown-text
msgid "the usual number of series and shots per series,"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:30
#, markdown-text
msgid "whole or decimal (up to 10.9) scoring and the highest value of a shot,"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:30
#, markdown-text
msgid "optionally a target face for tapping hits."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:31
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Weapons {#weapons}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:34
#, markdown-text
msgid "Shoot more than one gun, e.g. two air pistols? Add them under **Settings → Weapons** with a name of your choice; the calibre does not matter. Choose the weapon when you save a session and [Progress](progress.md#weapons-compared) compares them. Renaming a weapon keeps its sessions. Deleting it keeps the sessions too, they just have no weapon any more."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:35
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "API tokens"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:38
#, markdown-text
msgid "Want to import sessions from another app or analyse your log with your own script? Create a token in your account with the preset **Training app**; see [API tokens](../user-guide/login-language.md#api-tokens)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:39
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install the app"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "Standblatt is a web app that can be installed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:45
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Android / Chrome**: Settings → **Install**, or *Add to home screen* in the browser menu."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:45
#, markdown-text
msgid "**iPhone**: Share → *Add to Home Screen*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:47
#, markdown-text
msgid "Installed, it starts full screen. A long press on the icon offers *Start training*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:48
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Your data"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:51
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Export all sessions (CSV)** downloads every series of every session."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:51
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Delete account** on the [Account](../user-guide/login-language.md#account) page removes the account with all sessions, goals and settings after you enter your password. Accounts that belong to a club must first be removed from the club by its admin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Tutorial: your first training session"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "In this tutorial you log one air pistol training in My training: two series typed on the number pad and one series tapped on the target. Then you look at it in **Progress**. It takes about five minutes; a phone is ideal, but a computer works too."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "1. Create your account"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open Standblatt and click **Create an account** below the login. Enter your first name, last name, email address and a password of at least 10 characters, then tap **Create account**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "You are logged in and see **Today**. It says *Your log is empty — let's change that.*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "If your club already gave you an account, log in instead and choose **My training** on *Where to?*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:13
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2. Start the session"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "Tap **Log my first training**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "The session opens full screen. At the top you see the discipline *Air pistol 10 m*, below it the chips of five series of 10 shots, and the input **Series** is chosen. Leave everything as it is."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:19
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "3. Type two series"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid "Tap *9*, *2* on the number pad. Standblatt takes 92 for series 1 and jumps to series 2 by itself. Tap *8*, *9*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:24
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Series totals on the number pad](../images/screenshots/my-train-series.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "Chips 1 and 2 show 92 and 89, and series 3 is the current one. At the top you see the running total *181* with *20 shots · Ø 9.05*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:27
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "4. Tap a series on the target"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:30
#, markdown-text
msgid "Tap **Target** at the top right. A target face appears in place of the number pad."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid "Tap the target ten times, where your ten shots of this series hit. Every tap puts a hit on the target and its value in the row above it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:34
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Tapping hits on the target](../images/screenshots/my-train-target.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "After the tenth tap, chip 3 shows the total of your hits and series 4 becomes the current one. You stop here: series 4 and 5 stay empty and are left out when you save."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:37
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "5. Save with a tag"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid "Tap **Finish** at the top right. The sheet *Save session* opens; **Training** is chosen."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under **Tags**, type *new grip* in the field **New tag** and tap **+** next to it. The tag appears above the field, highlighted. Tap **Save session**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:44
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "![After saving](../images/screenshots/my-result.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:46
#, markdown-text
msgid "You see the total of the session with *30 shots* and the average per shot, and below it *Your first session in this format — the next one has something to beat.* Tap **Done** to return to **Today**: the session is listed under *Recent sessions*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:47
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "6. See your progress"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:50
#, markdown-text
msgid "Tap **Progress** in the bar at the bottom (on a computer it is in the sidebar). *Air pistol 10 m* is chosen."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:52
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Progress of a discipline](../images/screenshots/my-progress.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:58
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Last 30 days** shows the points per shot of your session."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:58
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Sessions** shows *1* and *30 shots*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:58
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Personal best** shows *–* with *50 shots*: it counts only sessions over the full 50 shots of the discipline."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:58
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Trend** shows your session as one dot. Every further session adds a dot, and the line through them shows where you are heading."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:58
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Series curve** compares your three series, **Shot values** counts the values of your ten tapped hits, and **Your group** shows where those hits sit on the target."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:62
#, markdown-text
msgid "You have logged a session in two ways of entering it, tagged it and seen it in your progress. Log the next training the same way; once two sessions carry the tag *new grip*, **Progress** shows under *What your tags tell you* whether the new grip pays off."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:67
#, markdown-text
msgid "Everything about entering and changing sessions: [Logging a session](logging.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:67
#, markdown-text
msgid "What every figure on **Progress** means: [Progress explained](progress.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/first-session.md:67
#, markdown-text
msgid "Add your birthday and license number to get your competition results: [Profile and competition results](account.md#competitions)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "My training"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "My training is a personal shooting diary. Every shooter can use it, whether or not their club runs events with Standblatt. It answers one question: **does my training work?**"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "New here? Start with [Tutorial: your first training session](first-session.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:8
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<div class=\"grid\" markdown>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Today on a phone](../images/screenshots/my-today.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Logging takes seconds.** After a session you tap the + button, type the series totals on the number pad and save. Standblatt moves on to the next series by itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid "**As detailed as you like.** Log only the series totals, every shot value, or tap every hit on the target. You can switch per series."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Feedback right away.** After saving you see how the session ranks among your sessions of the same length and how it compares with your last 30 days."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Progress you can read.** Trend, personal best, goal, series curve, shot values, the size and centre of your group, what your tags tell you and how your weapons compare."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Competitions come for free.** Results from events run with Standblatt are found by your license number and birthday once the club closes the event, and added with one tap, rank included."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Works at the range.** Install it on the home screen. Without signal, sessions are kept on the phone and uploaded later."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Your data stays yours.** Export everything as CSV at any time and delete your account whenever you want."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:23
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Pages"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:31
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Page | What it is for |\n|---|---|\n| **Today** | start a session, this week's activity, your recent trend and sessions |\n| **Log** | every session, filtered by discipline and kind, competition results waiting to be added |\n| **Progress** | the analysis of one discipline, see [Progress explained](progress.md) |\n| **Settings** | profile (name, birthday and license number for the competition match), own disciplines, weapons, app, export; **Account** for email, password, language, second factor and deleting the account |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:33
#, markdown-text
msgid "On a phone the pages are in the bar at the bottom, with the + button in the middle. On a larger screen they are in the sidebar."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:34
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Access and price"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "My training is free for every user of the server."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:38
#, markdown-text
msgid "Club staff accounts can use My training too: open **My training** in the user menu of the club sidebar."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Logging a session"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "Tap the **+** button, or a discipline under **Start training** on the Today page. The session opens full screen with your last discipline already selected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "At the top you see the running total, the number of shots and the average per shot. Below that is a chip for every series. Tap a chip to correct that series, tap **+** to add one, or use **Remove series** for the current one. The minus and plus next to \"10 shots\" change the number of shots of the current series, e.g. for a 5-shot series at 25 m."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:9
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Three ways to enter a series"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "Choose the input for the current series at the top right. You can mix them in one session, e.g. totals for the first four series and every shot for the last two."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:15
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Series**\n: Type the series total. As soon as no further digit could make the number valid, Standblatt takes it and jumps to the next series. \"9\", \"3\" gives 93 and moves on; a 100 needs \"1\", \"0\", \"0\". With decimal scoring the point is added for you: \"1\", \"0\", \"2\", \"7\" gives 102.7. **Next** takes the number as it is.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:18
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Shots**\n: Tap the value of every shot. With decimal scoring type two digits, e.g. \"9\", \"7\" for 9.7, or three for a ten, e.g. \"1\", \"0\", \"4\" for 10.4. After the last shot of a series the next series starts.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Target**\n: Tap where every shot hit. Standblatt computes the value from the target face of the discipline, with decimals if the discipline is scored that way. The magnifier switches between the black and the whole target. This is the only way to get the [group analysis](progress.md#group).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid "On a computer you can type the digits, **Backspace** and **Enter** on the keyboard; in **Shots** with whole-number scoring up to 10 only the buttons work (see [Keyboard](../reference/shortcuts.md#my-training))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:26
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Save"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid "When the last series is complete, or when you tap **Finish**, the save sheet opens. Everything in it is optional:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Training or competition**: competitions appear as their own dots in the trend and are compared with your training."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Weapon**: which of your [weapons](account.md#weapons) you shot with. A new session starts with the weapon of your last session in the same discipline; tap it again to clear it, or add a new weapon right there."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "**How did it feel?**: five faces from bad to great."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Tags**: short words for what was special, e.g. *new grip*, *tired*, *new pellets*. Progress compares the sessions with a tag to your average."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "**When**, **where**, **notes**. *Where* starts with the place of your last training."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:39
#, markdown-text
msgid "After saving Standblatt tells you right away:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "whether the session is a **new personal best**, or which place it takes among your sessions with the same number of shots;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "how many points per shot it is above or below the average of the **30 days before**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:43
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Unfinished sessions and offline {#unfinished-sessions-and-offline}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:46
#, markdown-text
msgid "The session is kept on the device while you type. If you close the browser or the phone locks, it comes back the next time you start a session."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:48
#, markdown-text
msgid "If there is no connection when you save, the session is kept on the device and uploaded as soon as you are online again. A note on the Today page shows how many sessions are waiting. A retried upload never creates a session twice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:50
#, markdown-text
msgid "Waiting sessions belong to the account that typed them. If your login expired in the meantime, log in again and they are uploaded; another person logging in on the same device does not get them. If the server refuses one, for example because its discipline was deleted, a note shows the reason and you can **Discard** it. Only new sessions can be saved offline; changing a session needs a connection."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:52
#, markdown-text
msgid "Once you opened the app online, it also opens without a connection and shows your last data."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:54
#, markdown-text
msgid "Why club work needs a connection and My training does not: [Offline](../explanation/data.md#offline)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:55
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Changing or deleting a session"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:57
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open the session in the **Log** and use the pencil to change it, or the bin to delete it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Progress explained"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:4
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Progress** analyses all sessions of one discipline; choose it at the top right. Everything is computed from the sessions in your log, nothing is estimated.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Progress](../images/screenshots/my-progress.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:7
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Points per shot"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "Sessions differ in length: a 50-shot match, two series after work, a 40-shot competition. Standblatt compares them by **points per shot**, the total divided by the number of shots. 9.30 per shot is 465 over 50 shots."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:11
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Key figures"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:15
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Last 30 days**\n: points per shot over all sessions of the last 30 days. The arrow shows the change against the 30 days before.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:18
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Personal best**\n: the highest total among sessions with the standard number of shots of the discipline, e.g. 50 for air pistol. Tap it to open the session.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Sessions**\n: number of sessions and shots logged in this discipline.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:24
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Competition vs. training**\n: points per shot in competitions minus points per shot in training. A negative number means you lose points under pressure.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:25
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Trend"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "Every session is a dot, competitions in amber. The line is the moving average of the last five sessions, so a single bad day does not hide the direction. A dashed line shows your goal."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:29
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Goal"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid "Set the total you want to reach over the standard number of shots, optionally with a date. The bar compares it with your last 30 days and tells you how much is missing per shot."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:33
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Series curve"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "Points per shot of the first, second, third … series over all sessions. It shows whether you need a series to warm up, or lose concentration towards the end. The strongest series is highlighted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:37
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Shot values"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid "How often each value occurred, from the sessions where you logged every shot or tapped the hits. Decimal values count towards their whole number, so 9.7 counts as a 9."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:41
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Group {#group}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:44
#, markdown-text
msgid "From the hits you tapped on the target in your last ten sessions with hits:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:48
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Group size** is twice the average distance of your hits from their centre, in mm. It is a robust measure of how tight you shoot."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:48
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Off centre** is the distance of that centre from the middle of the target."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:48
#, markdown-text
msgid "If the centre sits clearly to one side, Standblatt tells you which way to adjust the sight. Check your hold and trigger first."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:50
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Group on the target](../images/screenshots/my-session.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:51
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Weapons compared {#weapons-compared}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:54
#, markdown-text
msgid "As soon as sessions of a discipline were shot with at least two of your weapons, a table compares them: the points per shot of all their sessions, of the last 30 days and the best total over the full match. The weapon with the highest average is on top. Sessions without a weapon are not part of it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:56
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Two air pistols compared](../images/screenshots/my-weapons.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:58
#, markdown-text
msgid "Tap a weapon, or choose it in the weapon list at the top, and every figure on the page (key figures, trend, series curve, shot values and group) only counts the sessions shot with it. *All weapons* shows everything again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:59
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What your tags tell you"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:61
#, markdown-text
msgid "For every tag used on at least two sessions: the points per shot of those sessions and the difference to your overall average. Sorted from the best to the worst, this is where you find out whether the new grip pays off."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/reference/codes.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Codes and barcodes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/codes.md:3
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Registration code (QR)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/codes.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "Lane sheets and control strips carry a QR code with"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: ../src/help/en/reference/codes.md:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "REGCODEAAAA<registration>AAAAL<license or 0>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/codes.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "for example `REGCODEAAAA42AAAAL100109`. A hand scanner types it into the search field of the dashboard and presses Enter; Standblatt opens the results of that registration. The license part guards against a code from another shooter; a code of another event is refused."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/codes.md:13
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Programme barcode (Interleaved 2 of 5)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/codes.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "A programme can have a barcode, printed as Interleaved 2 of 5 next to the programme on the lane sheet (only the digits count, padded to an even number of digits). Electronic scoring systems use it to pick the programme."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "CSV import"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "Members with the permission *Manage master data* import shooters on the **Shooters** page. The file needs a header row; the separator (`;` or `,`) is taken from it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "license;firstname;lastname;birthday;postalcode;city;club\n100100;Sandra;Example;1969-06-02;9999;Hilltown;PS Example\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:18
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Column | Required | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `firstname` | yes | |\n| `lastname` | yes | |\n| `license` | no | also `licensenumber`; purely numeric numbers are padded to six digits |\n| `birthday` | no | `YYYY-MM-DD` or `DD.MM.YYYY` |\n| `postalcode`, `city` | no | |\n| `club` | no | the shooter's club, matched regardless of upper case and spaces |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid "One line per shooter and club; a shooter in two clubs appears twice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid "Shooters are matched by license number, or by name and birthday when there is none. Existing shooters are updated, nothing is deleted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid "A file with invalid lines is rejected as a whole, with the list of lines to fix."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid "Clubs that are not in the club list stop the import before anything is stored: for each one, choose an existing club (similar names are suggested) or a new one, then **Import** again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:24
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Results {#results}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid "Members with the permission *Configure events* import results with **Import CSV** on an event's **Enter results** page (see [Enter results](../user-guide/results-entry.md#import)):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:28
#, no-wrap
msgid "license;firstname;lastname;birthday;club;programme;s1;s2;m2;s1_1;s1_2;s1_3\n013756;;;;;Championship;96;93;2;;;\n;Max;Muster;1990-02-02;SG Hilltown;Obligatory;;45;;9;10;8\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:43
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Column | Required | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `license` or `firstname` + `lastname` | yes | the shooter: found by licence, else by name (and `birthday`, if several have the name); created when not found, which needs `firstname` and `lastname`: a licence alone that is not found is a line error |\n| `birthday` | no | `YYYY-MM-DD` or `DD.MM.YYYY` |\n| `club` | no | must be in the club list (regardless of upper case and spaces); the shooter joins it |\n| `programme` | yes | barcode, name with variant like `Championship (Sport)`, or the name alone |\n| `s1`, `s2`, … | yes | points per series, decimals with `.` or `,` |\n| `m1`, `m2`, … | no | mouches per series |\n| `s1_1`, `s1_2`, … | no | single shots of series 1, for series that record them; the series is their sum |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:47
#, markdown-text
msgid "Every line is checked first; with any line error nothing is imported."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:47
#, markdown-text
msgid "A shooter can have results in a programme only once; a line for results that exist already is an error. Programmes with several [attempts](../user-guide/programmes.md#attempts) take one line per attempt until the shooter has none left."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:47
#, markdown-text
msgid "For programmes with several attempts, importing the same file again adds its lines as further attempts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:47
#, markdown-text
msgid "If the shooter is registered for the programme without results, the results go into that registration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/reference/documents.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Documents and reports"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/documents.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "Every document is a PDF in the language of the event. A print goes to the printer set for the document on **Ranges → Set up the printers** of the registration's range when a print agent of the range is online; otherwise the PDF opens (see [Printing](../user-guide/printing.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/documents.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Documents {#documents}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/documents.md:18
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Document | Format | Content | Printed from | Printer setting | Module |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Lane sheet | A5 | event, shooter, QR [registration code](codes.md), range (events on several ranges), lane, programmes with shots and [barcodes](codes.md) | *Print lane sheet* at registration; the registration | *Lane sheet (A5)* | Lane sheet |\n| Control strip | label 90 × 29 mm, or a [print form](../user-guide/print-forms.md#builtin) of the club | event, shooter, licence, club, age category, passes, QR registration code | *Print control strip* at registration; the registration | *Control strip (label 90 × 29 mm)* | Control strip |\n| Result sheet | A5 | event, shooter, every programme with its series, total and award | **Print result sheet** in the results, once every programme has results | *Result sheet (A5)* | – |\n| Wreath card | A6, printed onto pre-printed cards, or a print form of the club | shooter, year of birth, club, date, organizer, value in figures and words (setting *Print the award value on wreath cards*) | **Print wreath card** in the results, for a wreath card award | *Wreath card (A6, pre-printed)* | Awards |\n| Print form of a programme | size of the form | see [Form placeholders](form-placeholders.md#results) | **Print onto form** in the results of a completed programme | *Print forms (pre-printed)* | club module Print forms |\n| Registration document | size of the form | see [Form placeholders](form-placeholders.md#registration) | a button named after the form in the registration | *Print forms (pre-printed)* | club module Print forms |\n| Certificates | size of the form, one page per ranked shooter | see [Form placeholders](form-placeholders.md#rank) | **Certificates** on **Rankings** | *Certificates* | club module Print forms |\n| Ranking | A4 | rank, name, year, category, club, series, total; ranks 1–3 highlighted; *(2/3)* for the counting attempt | **PDF** on **Rankings** and **Statistics** | never printed, PDF only | – |\n| Test page | label 90 × 29 mm | club, range, printer, options, time | **Test page** on **Ranges → Set up the printers** | the printer of that row | – |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/documents.md:22
#, markdown-text
