msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/permissions.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "**New role** starts with *See events and rankings* only."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/permissions.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "A role can be deleted once nobody has it; the admin role never."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/permissions.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "A club always keeps at least one member with the admin role."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/permissions.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "Members with *Users and club* but without the admin role give, change and remove only roles whose permissions they have themselves."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/permissions.md:38
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Helper links {#helper-links}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/permissions.md:41
#, markdown-text
msgid "Helper links are not roles of the club; each link has one of these roles (see [Creating a link](../user-guide/helpers.md#create)):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/permissions.md:47
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Role | Sees | Can |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Scorer** | the lane grid of their own lanes, the shooters on them | enter results and awards, **Finish** a shooter |\n| **Ammunition desk** | the search box, the waiting list, the shooters on all lanes | mark the ammunition as issued (**Ammo**), assign a lane to a waiting shooter, print the lane sheet |\n| **Results clerk** | the search box, the shooters on all lanes, the completed list | enter results and awards on every lane |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/permissions.md:49
#, markdown-text
msgid "Scorers and results clerks may also print [print forms](../user-guide/print-forms.md#use) of their lanes; a results clerk may mark awards as handed out."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/permissions.md:50
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "API token scopes {#scopes}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/permissions.md:53
#, markdown-text
msgid "A token (**Account** → **API tokens**, see [API tokens](../user-guide/login-language.md#api-tokens)) has a list of clubs and of scopes:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/permissions.md:59
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Scope | Key | Allows |\n|---|---|---|\n| *Read my training log* | `training:read` | read the own training log |\n| *Log and change my training sessions* | `training:write` | add, change and delete the own sessions, disciplines, weapons and goals |\n| a permission above | `events.view`, `events.operate`, `events.configure`, `reports.view`, `shooters.view`, `shooters.edit`, `shooters.manage`, `ranges.manage`, `forms.manage`, `club.manage` | the same as in a role, in the token's clubs |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/permissions.md:63
#, markdown-text
msgid "A club permission can only be chosen if the owner's role has it in one of the token's clubs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/permissions.md:63
#, markdown-text
msgid "A token never has more than the owner's role: a permission the role loses, or a club the owner leaves, is gone for the token at once."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/permissions.md:63
#, markdown-text
msgid "A token without clubs reaches only the training log."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: ../src/help/en/reference/permissions.md:64
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Presets {#presets}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/permissions.md:71
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Preset | Scopes |\n|---|---|\n| **Rankings for a website** | *See events and rankings* |\n| **Training app** | *Read my training log*, *Log and change my training sessions* |\n| **Read only** | *See events and rankings*, *Statistics and reports*, *See shooters and clubs*, *Read my training log* |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/permissions.md:73
#, markdown-text
msgid "A preset only fills in the permissions the chosen clubs allow."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: ../src/help/en/reference/permissions.md:74
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Using a token {#token-use}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/permissions.md:86
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| What | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Format | `sb_` and 40 hexadecimal digits, shown once |\n| Header | `Authorization: Bearer sb_…` or `X-API-Key: sb_…` |\n| Expires | in 30 or 90 days, in a year, or never |\n| Endpoints | `/api/tenants/…` (club data, by permission), `/api/my/…` (training log, by scope), `GET /api/token`, `/api/version`, `/api/auth/options`; with *Configure events* also `/api/modules` and `/api/programme-templates`; everything else answers 403 |\n| `GET /api/token` | the token's name, scopes and clubs |\n| Rate limit | by default 600 requests per token in five minutes, then 429; the operator changes it with `STANDBLATT_API_RATE_LIMIT` (0 = no limit) |\n| Unknown tokens | after 20 unknown or revoked tokens from one address in 15 minutes, 429 |\n| API description | `/api/docs` |\n| Never reachable | password, email, account settings, other tokens |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/reference/programme-file.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Programme file"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/programme-file.md:4
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Export** in the programme menu or on the programme page downloads a programme as `<name>.programme.json`; **Programme file** under *Add from …* imports it into another event or another club. The platform operator uploads the same files to the global programme library.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (json)
#: ../src/help/en/reference/programme-file.md:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "{\n  \"format\": \"standblatt.programme\",\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"programme\": {\n    \"name\": \"Championship\",\n    \"variant\": \"Sport\",\n    \"description\": \"\",\n    \"barcode\": \"700005002334864165956154\",\n    \"countsForClubCompetition\": true,\n    \"showOnRankings\": true,\n    \"series\": [\n      { \"shots\": 10, \"maxPoints\": 100, \"trackMouches\": false, \"name\": \"\" }\n    ],\n    \"prices\": [\n      { \"ageCategory\": \"elite\", \"price\": 20 }\n    ],\n    \"awards\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Wreath card CHF 10\",\n        \"kind\": \"card\",\n        \"value\": 10,\n        \"limits\": [{ \"ageCategory\": \"elite\", \"points\": 370 }]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/programme-file.md:38
#, markdown-text
msgid "`ageCategory` is one of `u10`, `u13`, `u15`, `u17`, `u19`, `u21`, `elite`, `senior`, `veteran`, `senior_veteran`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/programme-file.md:38
#, markdown-text
msgid "`kind` is `card` (wreath card, printed), `natural` (prize in kind) or `cash` (cash prize)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/programme-file.md:38
#, markdown-text
msgid "`showOnRankings` is the *Show on kiosk displays* switch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/programme-file.md:38
#, markdown-text
msgid "Optional fields: `attempts` (0 or left out = once), `unlimitedAttempts`, `attemptRule` (`best`, `first` or `last`) and `awardCountingOnly` for [attempts](../user-guide/programmes.md#attempts); `repeatPrice` in a price (left out = the same price, 0 = paid once); `trackShots` in a series for single shots."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/programme-file.md:38
#, markdown-text
msgid "Combinations and special prizes are settings of the programme within an event and are not part of the file; copying programmes from an earlier event keeps them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Competition rules"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "This page describes the rules exactly as Standblatt implements them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Age category {#age-categories}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "The category follows from *event year − birth year*. Without a birthday a shooter counts as Elite. The category is fixed when the shooter registers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Category | Short | Age in the event year |\n|---|---|---|\n| U10 | U10 | up to 9 |\n| U13 | U13 | 10–12 |\n| U15 | U15 | 13–14 |\n| U17 | U17 | 15–16 |\n| U19 | U19 | 17–18 |\n| U21 | U21 | 19–20 |\n| Elite | E | 21–45 |\n| Senior | S | 46–59 |\n| Veteran | V | 60–69 |\n| Senior veteran | SV | 70 and older |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid "The event year is the year of the event's main day, also for shooting days in another year."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:24
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Registration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid "A registration is refused when:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:34
#, markdown-text
msgid "a programme does not belong to the event, is chosen twice or is not active, or more attempts are chosen than it allows;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:34
#, markdown-text
msgid "a programme has no price for the shooter's age category (\"not open to the age category\");"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:34
#, markdown-text
msgid "two variants of the same programme are chosen;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:34
#, markdown-text
msgid "a programme takes series from another programme that is not chosen, or the number of picked series does not match;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:34
#, markdown-text
msgid "the lane is taken by another active registration or is out of service;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:34
#, markdown-text
msgid "the shooter is already registered for one of the programmes at this event (a shooter shoots each programme once per event unless it allows several [attempts](../user-guide/programmes.md#attempts); another variant in a separate registration is fine)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "A reserved lane can still be used after a confirmation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:37 ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Results"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid "Every series must be entered. Points lie between 0 and the series maximum (by default shots × 10), mouches between 0 and the number of shots, and only on series that track mouches. Saving results gives the most valuable award the total reaches; saving them again keeps the chosen award as long as the new total still reaches it, otherwise the most valuable one reached. Once every programme of a registration has results, the registration is completed and its lane becomes free."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:41
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Combinations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:44
#, markdown-text
msgid "A programme marked *combinable with* another programme can take series from it: at registration the shooter picks which series (for example series 2 and 3 of a four-series programme for a two-series programme). The picked series are copied in ascending order and renumbered from 1; the combined programme cannot be edited on its own and follows every change of the source."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:45 ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Awards"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:48
#, markdown-text
msgid "An award tier is available to an age category only if it has a limit for it. A shooter can choose any tier whose limit the total reaches; the most valuable tier is listed first and given by default when the results are saved. The server checks the choice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:49
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Ranking {#ranking}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:52
#, markdown-text
msgid "All results of a programme are ordered by:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:57
#, markdown-text
msgid "higher total;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:57
#, markdown-text
msgid "the series compared from the last one backwards (the better last series wins, then the second-to-last, …);"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:57
#, markdown-text
msgid "more mouches;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:57
#, markdown-text
msgid "age: among juniors (U10–U21) the younger shooter first, among the others the older shooter first; non-juniors rank before juniors."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:59
#, markdown-text
msgid "Ranks are consecutive (1, 2, 3, … even on equal results). The same ranking feeds the staff pages, kiosk screens, the ranking PDF and CSV, and special prizes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:63
#, markdown-text
msgid "Only programmes marked *counts for the club competition* take part, and only completed results of shooters with a club."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:70
#, markdown-text
msgid "The score of a result is the sum of its first two series."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:70
#, markdown-text
msgid "A club with fewer than 5 participants is listed as *not ranked*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:70
#, markdown-text
msgid "Of *n* participants the best *max(5, ⌊n/2⌋)* are mandatory, the rest are optional."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:70
#, markdown-text
msgid "Result = ⌊(Σ mandatory + 0.02 × Σ optional) / number of mandatory × 1000⌋ / 1000, i.e. truncated to three decimals."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:70
#, markdown-text
msgid "Ties: more participants first, then the sorted scores compared one by one."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:70
#, markdown-text
msgid "The club excluded in the settings of the module *Club competition* (usually the host) keeps its place in the list but gets no rank (\"out of competition\")."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:74
#, markdown-text
msgid "A programme can award special prizes to the best ranks of every age category. Three numbers define them:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:78
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Ranks per category**, e.g. 3;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:78
#, markdown-text
msgid "**minimum participants per category** in this programme, e.g. 10;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:78
#, markdown-text
msgid "**minimum participants of the shooter's club** in the same programme, e.g. 4."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:80
#, markdown-text
msgid "Per age category with enough participants, the first shooters in ranking order whose club has enough participants win; shooters whose club has too few are skipped and the next one moves up. Shooters without a club are not eligible unless the club minimum is 0. The report lists both the winners and the skipped shooters with the reason."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:83
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "!!! example \"From the brochure to the settings\"\n    A brochure says: *\"In every category, ranks 1–3 receive a special prize, provided the category has at least 10 participants and the shooter's club at least 4.\"* That is ranks 3, category minimum 10, club minimum 4.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:84
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Lane lists"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:87
#, markdown-text
msgid "Lanes are written as a list of numbers and ranges: `1, 5, 7-10`. Standblatt prints them compactly, turning runs of three or more into ranges (`1-3, 5, 7, 8`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:88
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Money and numbers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:90
#, markdown-text
msgid "Amounts are shown as `CHF 1'234.50`, dates as `dd.mm.yyyy`. On wreath cards the value can be printed in words in the event's language, e.g. *Fünfundzwanzig Franken*, *Septante et un francs*, *Ventitré franchi*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/reference/shortcuts.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Keyboard and scanner"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/shortcuts.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "On a Mac, Cmd works wherever Ctrl is listed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/shortcuts.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Dashboard {#dashboard}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/shortcuts.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "Also on helper links with a search box (ammunition desk, results clerk)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/shortcuts.md:14
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Key | Does |\n|---|---|\n| F4 | clear the search field and jump into it |\n| Esc | clear the search field |\n| Enter after a [registration code](codes.md) | open the results of that registration; a code of another event or another shooter is refused |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/shortcuts.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "A hand scanner types the QR code of a lane sheet or control strip followed by Enter, so scanning opens the results directly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/shortcuts.md:17
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Result fields {#results}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/shortcuts.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "In the results of a registration, on **Enter results** and on scorer links."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/shortcuts.md:25
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Key | Does |\n|---|---|\n| digits | the cursor moves to the next field as soon as another digit would exceed the maximum of the series, the shot or the mouches |\n| Enter | save the programme |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/shortcuts.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid "So `96 93 97 88` can be typed without the mouse. After the last field the cursor moves to **Save**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/shortcuts.md:28
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Enter results {#quick-entry}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/shortcuts.md:35
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Key | Does |\n|---|---|\n| Enter in **Shooter** | search at once and take the first hit |\n| Esc in **Shooter** | clear the field |\n| Enter in the results | save the result and get ready for the next shooter |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/shortcuts.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "A barcode scanner that types the licence number and Enter picks the shooter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/shortcuts.md:38
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "My training {#my-training}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/shortcuts.md:41
#, markdown-text
msgid "While a session is open on a computer, unless the focus is in a text field:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/shortcuts.md:48
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Key | Does |\n|---|---|\n| 0–9 | type the series total or the shot value |\n| . or , | decimal point |\n| Backspace | delete the last digit; with nothing typed, take back the last value |\n| Enter | take the number as it is, like **Next** |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/shortcuts.md:50
#, markdown-text
msgid "With whole-number scoring up to 10, shot values are tapped on the buttons; the keyboard types series totals there."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/shortcuts.md:51
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Print form editor {#print-forms}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/shortcuts.md:54
#, markdown-text
msgid "Except while typing in a field; Ctrl+S works there too."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/shortcuts.md:67
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Key | Does |\n|---|---|\n| Arrow keys | move the selection by 0.5 mm, with Shift by 5 mm |\n| Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y | undo / redo |\n| Ctrl+Shift+Z | redo |\n| Ctrl+A | select everything |\n| Ctrl+D | duplicate |\n| Delete or Backspace | delete the selection |\n| Esc | clear the selection |\n| Ctrl+S | save |\n| Ctrl+mouse wheel | zoom |\n| Shift or Ctrl and click | add an element to the selection or remove it |\n| Alt while dragging | place freely, without snapping |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/classifications.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Classifications"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/classifications.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "A programme ranking ranks one programme. A **classification** ranks shooters over several programmes or over several [attempts](programmes.md#attempts) of one programme, e.g. a section championship as the sum of three programmes, or a club championship over the best three attempts of an annual programme. Classifications appear on **Rankings**, on kiosk displays and as a report; how they relate to the programme rankings is explained in [How rankings fit together](../explanation/rankings.md#classifications)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/classifications.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Create a classification {#create}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/classifications.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "With the module *Classifications* switched on (**Configuration** → **Modules**), **New classification** on **Classifications** in the configuration (admins) opens the editor:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/classifications.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Programmes**: every programme that counts, with its **Counting attempts**. With 3, the best three attempts count (or the first or last three, as set by the programme's *Counting attempt*). A shooter's total is the sum of all counted attempts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/classifications.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Count only the best programmes**: with several programmes, only that many with the highest points count, e.g. the best two of three; 0 counts all."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/classifications.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Rank only shooters with all counting results**: shooters who are still missing a programme or an attempt are listed below the ranking without a rank. Without it everybody is ranked by what they have."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/classifications.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Tie-break**: equal totals are decided by the ticked criteria in their order; the arrows change it. *Series from the last one backwards* compares all counted series, *More of the highest single shots* needs [single shots](programmes.md) (more tens, then more nines …), *Age* follows the [SSV rule](../reference/rules.md#ranking). The default is the SSV order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/classifications.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Classes**: separate rankings, each for some age categories, e.g. *Juniors* with U17 to U21 and *Elite* with the others. An age category belongs to one class at most; shooters whose category is in no class are not listed. Without classes everybody is in one ranking."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/classifications.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Show on kiosk displays**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/classifications.md:16
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Examples {#examples}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/classifications.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Event | Programmes | Settings |\n|---|---|---|\n| Shooting festival, best two stiche | three stiche | *Count only the best programmes* 2 |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/classifications.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid "Step by step: [Rank a section championship over several programmes](../how-to/section-championship.md) and [Run an annual programme over the season](../how-to/annual-programme.md#classification)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/classifications.md:24
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Copy for next year** copies the classifications with the programmes. Deleting a programme removes it from the classifications.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Dashboard"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "The dashboard is the desk view of an event: who is shooting on which lane, who is waiting, who is done."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Shooting**: registrations on a lane, with the time since they started, the buttons **Results**, **Edit** and **Finish**. When the module *Ammunition desk* is on, **Ammo** records that it was handed out and a green *ammo* badge shows it afterwards (see [Helpers](helpers.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Waiting**: registrations without a lane (for example when all lanes are taken). Without [lane assignment](events.md#modules) (or without a range) there are no lanes and no *Shooting*: the list is called **Registered** and offers **Results**, **Edit** and **Finish**; a registration leaves it once its results are complete."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Completed**: registrations whose programmes all have results, with an *awards to hand out* badge that opens the results dialog for the handout, or *awards handed out* afterwards (see [Results](results.md#handout))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Lanes**: every lane is *free*, *occupied* (with the shooter), *reserved* (with the reservation and its end) or *out of service*. A reservation shows from its lead time on. An event on several ranges shows one grid per range, and the registration dialog groups the lanes by range; a shooter who moves to another range is finished and registered again there."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "The figures at the top count waiting, shooting and completed registrations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "*Waiting* and *Completed* show 50 registrations per page; the arrows below the list turn the pages."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "Everything updates live; the dot next to **live** in the header shows the connection (see [Live updates](../explanation/data.md#live)). Without a connection a red bar says so and nothing can be saved (see [Offline](../explanation/data.md#offline))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:16
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Search and scan"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "Press ++f4++ anywhere on the dashboard to jump into the search field."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Search](../images/screenshots/search.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "Type a **license number** (digits only, leading zeros optional), a **name** (part of first or last name) or **first and last name** in either order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "Each hit offers **Register for &lt;club&gt;** for every club of the shooter, or **Open registration** if the shooter is currently registered."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "**New shooter** creates a shooter and opens the registration right away."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "A hand scanner reading the [registration code](../reference/codes.md) on a lane sheet or control strip types the code and Enter: the results of that registration open directly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "All keys: [Keyboard and scanner](../reference/shortcuts.md#dashboard)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:29
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Finish shooting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:31
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Finish** ends a registration before all results are in, for example when a shooter gives up or hands in the targets later. The registration moves to *Completed* and its lane becomes free; missing results can still be entered.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Events"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:4
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Events** lists the events of the club in the groups *Today* (between the first and the last shooting day), *Upcoming*, *Past* and *Closed*; roles with the permission *Configure events* create new ones there. Opening an event shows its dashboard and the other pages of the operation in the sidebar; *Change event* at the top of the sidebar returns to the list.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Events](../images/screenshots/events.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "An event has two areas. The **operation** is what you work with on the day: *Dashboard*, *Enter results*, *Rankings*, *Statistics* and the pages of switched-on modules such as *Reservations*. **Configuration** at the end of the sidebar (admins only) opens the set-up of the event; the sidebar then lists its pages, and *Back to the event* returns to the operation:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:18
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Page | What it holds |\n|---|---|\n| **General** | name, days, ranges, organizer and language (see below) |\n| **Modules** | the building blocks the event uses (see below) |\n| **Programmes** | what can be shot (see [Programmes](programmes.md)) |\n| Pages of modules | e.g. **Reservations** (with the online booking), **Classifications**, **Kiosk displays**, **Helper links**, only while the module is on |\n| **Copy & close** | copy for next year, close, reopen and delete |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "The configuration needs the permission *Configure events*, the operation *Run events* (see [Roles](users.md#roles)). Why the two are separate: [Configuration and operation](../explanation/modules.md#configuration)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Settings {#settings}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:24
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**General** holds what every event has:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:32
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Setting | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| Name, Date, Ranges | the date is the main day; its year sets the age categories (SSV: competition year minus year of birth, the day itself does not matter, which counts for pre-shooting days in December before a January event); tick every range the event is shot on, or none for an event without lanes (see below) |\n| Shooting days | single days with optional shooting times, for pre-shooting days and multi-day events (registrations count on the day they are made); the main day is always one |\n| Period (season) | for events over weeks or months, e.g. the Feldschiessen from the opening of the range until 31 August: first and last day, plus the weekdays with their shooting times; no weekday ticked means every day. Single days, e.g. the official weekend, add to the period or replace its times on that date |\n| Organizer | printed on documents |\n| Language of documents and kiosk | language of PDFs, CSV exports and kiosk screens, independent of each user's interface language |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:34
#, markdown-text
msgid "Shooting times also give the online booking its slots, unless the booking sets other hours for a day (see [Online booking](online-booking.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "Step by step for a season: [Run an annual programme over the season](../how-to/annual-programme.md), [Set up a Feldschiessen over a period](../how-to/feldschiessen.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:37
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Modules {#modules}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:40
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Modules** switches the building blocks of the event on and off; why events differ only by their modules is explained in [Modules and kinds of events](../explanation/modules.md).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "![The modules of an event](../images/screenshots/modules.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:44
#, markdown-text
msgid "Every module is a card with its switch; the settings of a module, e.g. *Print the award value on wreath cards* of *Awards*, sit on its card. What every module adds, its settings and when it stays on: [Modules](../reference/modules.md#event-modules)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:46
#, markdown-text
msgid "When you create an event, choose what kind it is; this only switches modules on (see [Event kinds](../reference/modules.md#kinds))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:48
#, markdown-text
msgid "A module that holds data stays on, and the card says why its switch is locked (see [Why a module that holds data stays on](../explanation/modules.md#in-use)). A module another one needs, e.g. *Awards* for *Special prizes* or *Lane assignment* for *Reservations*, stays on as long as that one is."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:52
#, markdown-text
msgid "Some modules belong to the club rather than to an event. **Club modules** in the club part of the sidebar (permission *Users and club*) switches them on and off; for now that is *Print forms* (see [Print forms](print-forms.md)). What each adds and when it stays on: [Club modules](../reference/modules.md#club-modules); why they belong to the club: [Club modules and event modules](../explanation/modules.md#club-modules)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:53
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Events without lanes {#no-lanes}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:56
#, markdown-text
msgid "An event without lanes has no range, or switches *Lane assignment* off; what each choice means is explained in [Events with and without lanes](../explanation/modules.md#lanes)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:57
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Copy for next year {#copy}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:60
#, markdown-text
msgid "On **Copy & close** in the configuration, **Copy** under *Copy for next year* creates a new event with the same ranges, organizer, language, settings, modules and all programmes, including prices, awards, combinations and special prizes, and the [classifications](classifications.md); the shooting days and the period move with the date, weekly shooting times stay on their weekdays. Registrations, results, kiosk links, helper links and the booking link are not copied. The dialog *Copy event* suggests the name and the date one year later; **Create copy** creates the event. Step by step: [Take over last year's event](../how-to/next-year.md#copy)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:62
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Copy an event](../images/screenshots/copy-event.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:63
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Templates {#templates}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:66
#, markdown-text
msgid "An event that is set up well can become a **template** of the club: **Save as template** on **Copy & close** stores a copy with its modules, settings, ranges, programmes and classifications, named after the event without its year. Templates are listed under *Templates* below the events; a template opens in its configuration and can be changed like an event, but it takes no registrations. **New event** lists the club's templates below the kinds (see [Start from a template of the club](../how-to/next-year.md#template)). **Delete** on the template's **Copy & close** removes it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:68
#, markdown-text
msgid "![New event with the kinds and a template of the club](../images/screenshots/new-event.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:69
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Close {#close}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:72
#, markdown-text
msgid "When an event is over and the rankings are checked, **Close event** on **Copy & close** in the configuration closes it; a banner on every page of the event then says so, and **Reopen** makes it editable again. What closing means for the rankings, My training and changes: [Closing an event](../explanation/closing.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:73
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Delete"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:75
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Delete** (on **Copy & close**) removes an event, but only while nobody is registered for it. A closed event cannot be deleted; reopen it first.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Helpers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "Helpers at the event (scorers, the ammunition desk, the results office) work with a **helper link** instead of a login. A helper link opens a reduced desk of one event on any phone or laptop; admins switch on the module *Helper links* under **Configuration** → **Modules**, create the links on **Helper links** in the configuration and revoke them when the event is over."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Scorer's helper page on a phone](../images/screenshots/helper-scorer.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:7 ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:16
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Roles {#roles}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "A link is a **Scorer** (their own lanes), the **Ammunition desk** or a **Results clerk** (all lanes). What each role sees and can do: [Helper links](../reference/permissions.md#helper-links)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "Everything else stays with the club's users: registering shooters, editing programmes, rankings, statistics, deleting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:13
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Creating a link {#create}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "Enter a name (who gets the link, e.g. *Scorer range A*), choose the role and, for a scorer, the range and the lanes (`1-5, 8`). One scorer usually looks after several lanes; scorers exist only while the event assigns lanes (module *Lane assignment*)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Create helper link**; copy the link and send it to the helper (e.g. by messenger). It is shown only once."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "The helper opens the link; it stays valid until it is revoked or the event is deleted. Its language can be changed in the link (see [URL parameters](../reference/links.md#parameters))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:20
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**revoke** in the list stops a link immediately; *last seen* tells when it was last used. A scorer who opens a shooter on another lane gets *This lane is not yours*.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Ammunition {#ammunition}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:23
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Ammo** on a waiting or shooting registration records the time the ammunition was handed out; the button exists only when the module *Ammunition desk* is on (air pistol and air rifle shooters usually bring their own). The dashboard shows a green *ammo* badge on such registrations, so the desk and the range officer see at a glance who has been served.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Login and language"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:3
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Logging in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "Log in with your email address (or user name) and password: you chose the password when you accepted the invitation of your club, or you received it from your club admin or the platform operator. Club accounts are not created by sign-up; only [My training](../my-training/account.md) has its own sign-up. Logged in, you change your password yourself under [Account](#account)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "After the login you land on the start page with a card for every club you belong to and one for [My training](../my-training/index.md), which every user has; **Account** and **Log out** are below the cards. Without a club membership the start page takes you straight to My training."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Login](../images/screenshots/login.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Start page](../images/screenshots/home.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "A login stays valid for seven days of inactivity and at most 30 days; with **Stay logged in for 90 days** ticked, it lasts 90 days on that device. After too many failed attempts, logins from the same address are blocked for a while."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "If your account belongs to several clubs, you choose the club after logging in; **Switch club** in the user menu goes back to that choice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:17
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Forgotten password {#password}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "If your account has a confirmed email address, use **Forgot your password?** on the login page. You get a link that is valid for one hour. Setting a new password logs you out everywhere. Without a confirmed email address, ask the operator to set a new password in the admin panel."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Account {#account}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:24
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Account** in the user menu (bottom of the sidebar), on the start page and in My training's sidebar opens your account settings:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Login**: your user name (it cannot be changed) and your email address. **Add** or **Change** asks for your password and sends a confirmation link; until you confirm, the address counts as *not confirmed* and **Send again** sends a new link. A confirmed address lets you reset a forgotten password yourself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Password**: enter the current and the new password (at least 10 characters). Other devices are logged out, the one you are on stays."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Language and theme**: the interface language of your account and light or dark mode."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Second factor**: see below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "**API tokens**: see below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Delete account**: only for accounts that belong to no club; the training log, goals and settings are deleted for good. Club accounts are removed by the club admin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:34
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "API tokens {#api-tokens}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "Want to show the rankings on the club website, import sessions from another app or analyse data with your own script? Create a token under **Account → API tokens** with **New token**:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid "a **name** that tells you later what uses it,"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid "a **preset** fills in the permissions for a common use: **Rankings for a website**, **Training app** or **Read only** (see [Presets](../reference/permissions.md#presets)),"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid "the **clubs** the token may use (none: only your training log),"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid "the **permissions**: *Read my training log*, *Log and change my training sessions* and, for the chosen clubs, the [permissions of roles](users.md#roles) your own role has there,"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid "when it **expires**: in 30 or 90 days, in a year, or never."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:45
#, markdown-text
msgid "The token (`sb_…`) is shown only once; copy it right away. It may do what you chose and never more than your role in the club: if you lose a permission or leave the club, the token loses it at once. It never reaches your password, email, account or other tokens. The list shows when each token was last used; revoking one stops it at once. How scripts send it, what it reaches and its limits: [Using a token](../reference/permissions.md#token-use)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:46
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Second factor {#totp}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:49
#, markdown-text
msgid "An authenticator app can protect your login with a six-digit code after the password; to set it up, switch it off or recover from a lost phone see [Protect your login with a second factor](../how-to/two-factor.md). The operator can also switch the feature off for the whole server."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:50
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Language"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:53
#, markdown-text
msgid "The interface is available in English, German, French and Italian. Without a choice, Standblatt follows the browser's language. **Language** in the user menu (bottom of the sidebar) sets it for your account on every device."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:55
#, markdown-text
msgid "Printed documents, CSV exports and kiosk screens do not follow your choice but the language of the event, so that every printout of an event looks the same (see [Events](events.md#settings))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:56
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Dark mode"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:59
#, markdown-text
msgid "The sun/moon button in the header switches between light and dark mode; the choice is kept in the browser."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:61
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Dashboard in dark mode](../images/screenshots/dashboard-dark.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:62
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Version"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:64
#, markdown-text
msgid "The bottom of the sidebar shows the version of the server, which helps when reporting a problem; in My training on a phone it is under **Settings**. When a new version is released, open pages offer **Reload** within a minute and load it on the next page change at the latest."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Online booking"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "With **online booking**, external clubs ask for lanes themselves. The organizer puts a link into the invitation; a club picks the time slots it wants, says how many lanes it needs in each and announces its shooters. An admin confirms or declines every request."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Switching it on {#setup}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "The online booking is part of the module *Reservations* (it needs a range and *Lane assignment*): on **Reservations** in the configuration, **Switch on** is all it takes. The page then shows the link with a QR code for the invitation and the slots it offers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Online booking in the configuration](../images/screenshots/booking-setup.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "Without changes, every day of the event is open during its shooting times (see [Events](events.md#settings)), or from 08:00 to 17:00 when it has none, in slots of 30 minutes, and requests are accepted until 14 days before the first day. **Adjust** changes this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Shooting from** and **Shooting until**: the hours of every day without shooting times."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Break from** and **Break until**: an optional break, e.g. for lunch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Slot length (minutes)**: how long one slot is."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Lanes per slot and club**: a limit per request; empty means no limit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Deadline**: the last day clubs can ask or change their request."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Days with other hours**: one line per day of the event, e.g. Friday 17:00–20:00. The days come from the event and follow it when you add or remove one."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**New link** replaces the link; the old one stops working. **Switch off** closes the booking; requests and confirmed reservations stay. *Copy for next year* takes the hours along, but not the link and not the deadline.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:22
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What a club sees {#club}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid "The link opens a page without login. It shows the event, the deadline and every slot with the lanes still free on each range. Only confirmed reservations count; names of other clubs are never shown."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid "![The booking page of a club](../images/screenshots/booking-public.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid "The club enters the number of lanes per slot, its name, a contact person, email and phone, and its **Shooters**: last name, first name, birthday and optionally the licence. **Paste list** takes rows copied from Excel (last name, first name, birthday, licence). The shooter list can follow later; programmes are chosen at the range as usual."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "After **Send request**, the club gets a mail with a personal link. Through it, it can check the status, change the request or cancel it until the deadline. Changing the slots of a confirmed request releases its lanes and the request waits for a new confirmation; adding shooters keeps it confirmed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:32
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Confirming requests {#confirm}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "Every admin with an email gets a mail for each new, changed or cancelled request. The requests are listed at the top of **Reservations**; the sidebar shows how many are waiting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Booking requests on the reservations page](../images/screenshots/booking-requests.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Confirm** gives each slot free lanes of its range, neighbours where possible, as an ordinary reservation named after the club, and mails the lane numbers to the club. When a slot has too few free lanes, nothing is reserved and the message names the slot; move a reservation or decline."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Confirm** first asks which **Club** of the master data the request belongs to, because the club typed its name itself: the club with the same name is chosen already, clubs with a similar name are suggested, and *New club* creates it. The request then shows the club it was matched to."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Confirm** also takes the shooters into the master data, in that club: a shooter is found by licence, else by name and birthday, and created otherwise. Existing shooters are never overwritten, because the list comes from a public form; only a missing birthday or licence is filled in. Shooters added after the confirmation are taken over with **Take over shooters**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Decline** asks for an optional reason, which goes to the club by mail. Lanes the request held are free again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid "The reserved lanes are ordinary [reservations](reservations.md): change their lane numbers there if needed. At the event, the shooters are found with the normal search at the registration desk. The report *Lane bookings* under [Statistics and reports](statistics-reports.md) lists every club with its slots, lanes and shooters."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Print forms"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "A print form puts results onto a pre-printed sheet, e.g. the lane sheets the army supplies for the obligatory programme: the shots are entered at the lane or afterwards, and the sheet is printed instead of filled in by hand. Filling in sheets by hand stays possible; print forms are optional and can be switched off under **Club modules** (see [Club modules](events.md#club-modules))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "Why and how print forms work: [Print forms on pre-printed sheets](../explanation/printing.md#forms)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:7
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Create a form {#create}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:10
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Print forms** (permission *Print forms*, in the club part of the sidebar) lists the forms of the club. **New print form** asks for a name, what the form **Prints** (see [Data source](#source)) and a paper size, then opens the editor. It has three columns:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:17
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Fields** on the left: everything a form can print, in groups, with an example each and a search. A click adds the field below the lowest element; dragging it onto the sheet puts it where you drop it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:17
#, markdown-text
msgid "*Own text* prints fixed text, *QR code* and *Barcode* print their value as a code, *Line* draws a line."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:17
#, markdown-text
msgid "*Shooter*, *Club and event* and *Result* print one value each, e.g. the name, the total or the points of a series."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:17
#, markdown-text
msgid "*Single shots* adds a whole row of shot boxes: *Shots of series 1* is one element `{{s1.shot#}}` repeated once per shot, 8 mm apart."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:17
#, markdown-text
msgid "The **Sheet** in the middle shows the form true to scale over the scan, with made-up values; **Show field names** shows the placeholders instead. Rulers in millimetres run along the top and the left, the zoom goes from 50 to 200 %."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:17
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Properties** on the right edit the selected element exactly: its **Value** (placeholders such as `{{shooter.name}}` are filled in when printing), **x** and **y** in millimetres from the top left corner, **Width** and **Height** (a width of 0 lets text run to the right edge), **Font size**, **Bold**, **Italic**, **Wrap text** (the text breaks into lines within the width, each as high as the height) and **Alignment**. **Repeat** prints it several times, moved by **dx** and **dy** each time; `#` in a placeholder counts 1, 2, 3, …. Below, the **Form** sets the name, the size of the sheet, the printer offset and the **Scan of the empty form**: a PNG or JPEG of the whole sheet that appears behind the sheet so the fields can be placed onto the boxes of the form; it is never printed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:19
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Save** stores the form; a dot on the button shows unsaved changes, and leaving the page with them asks first. With **Save automatically** (on unless you switch it off; the browser remembers it) unsaved changes are stored every minute. **PDF preview** opens the saved form exactly as the PDF renders it, which can differ slightly from the sheet in the browser.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:20
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Data source {#source}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid "What a form **Prints** decides its fields and where it is printed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:29
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Prints | Fields | Printed from |\n|---|---|---|\n| Results of a programme | shooter, club, event, series, single shots, total, award and its value | the results of a programme (see [Use a form](#use)) or as the event's wreath card |\n| A registration | shooter, club, event, lane, programmes, passes, QR code of the registration | as the event's control strip |\n| A rank | shooter, club, event, rank, total, ranking, class | certificates from the rankings |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "The source can be changed in the editor under **Form**; fields the new source does not know print nothing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:33
#, markdown-text
msgid "Every placeholder: [Form placeholders](../reference/form-placeholders.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:34
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Built-in forms {#builtin}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "Standblatt prints the wreath card and the control strip with **built-in forms**, listed below the forms of the club. **Copy** turns one into a form of the club that can be changed like any other, e.g. to move the fields onto another pre-printed wreath card or to add the club's logo. An event then chooses it under **Configuration** → **Modules**: *Print form of the wreath cards* in the module *Awards*, *Print form of the control strips* in the module *Control strip*. Without a choice, or when the chosen form is deleted, the built-in form prints."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:39
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Print forms with the built-in forms and the image library](../images/screenshots/print-forms.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:40
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Registration documents and certificates {#certificates}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid "A form that prints **A registration** besides the event's control strip, e.g. a participant card or a receipt, appears in the registration with a button of its own name; it prints on the printer of *Print forms (pre-printed)*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:45
#, markdown-text
msgid "A form that prints **A rank** makes certificates through **Certificates** on **Rankings**, printed on the printer of *Certificates* of the event's first range; see [Print certificates for the best ranks](../how-to/certificates.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:48
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Arrange the elements {#arrange}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:54
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Move** an element by dragging it, **resize** it by its corner. The pink dot on the last box of a repeated element drags the spacing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:54
#, markdown-text
msgid "While moving, the element **snaps** to the edges and centres of the other elements and of the sheet, and a pink guide shows the line; elsewhere it snaps to whole millimetres. Hold Alt to place it freely."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:54
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Select several** with Shift or Ctrl and a click, or draw a frame around them on the empty sheet. Dragging moves them together; font size, bold and alignment then apply to all of them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:54
#, markdown-text
msgid "A **right click** opens the menu: *Duplicate*, *Bring to front*, *Align* (edges, centres, distribute evenly), *Centre on the sheet* and *Delete*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:56
#, markdown-text
msgid "Keys: [Print form editor](../reference/shortcuts.md#print-forms)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:57
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Images {#images}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:60
#, markdown-text
msgid "Logos, letterheads and other pictures come from the club's image library below the list of **Print forms**: **Upload image** adds a PNG or JPEG of at most 2 MB, named after its file. In the editor, the group **Images** of the fields lists them; a click or a drag puts one onto the sheet, 30 mm wide with the image's own proportions. Its properties choose another **Image**, its position and size, and **Keep the aspect ratio** sets the height to match the width again. An image can be repeated like any other element."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:62
#, markdown-text
msgid "An image can be deleted only while no form shows it. **Export** puts the images of a form into its file, and **Import** adds them to the library, reusing an image of the same name the club already has."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:63
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Calibrate the printer {#calibrate}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:66
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Printer offset right (mm)** and **Printer offset down (mm)** under **Form** move every element (negative to move left or up). **Test print** opens the saved form with the offset and without the scan; the preview ignores the offset. Why: [Calibration in principle](../explanation/printing.md#calibration). Steps: [Print results onto the army's lane sheets](../how-to/army-sheet.md#calibrate).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:67
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Use a form {#use}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:70
#, markdown-text
msgid "A programme chooses its form in the section **Print form** of its programme page, also while shooters are registered. Completed results then offer **Print onto form**: in the results at the desk, in *Entered now* on **Enter results** and on helper links of scorers and results clerks (see [Helpers](helpers.md)). It prints on the printer of *Print forms (pre-printed)* of the registration's range, otherwise the PDF opens (see [Printing](printing.md)). Steps: [Print results onto the army's lane sheets](../how-to/army-sheet.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:71
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Export** downloads a form as a file, with its images, and **Import** reads it again, e.g. to share a form with another club.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:1
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:26
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Printing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "Standblatt renders all documents as PDF. Every document with its format, content and printer setting: [Documents](../reference/documents.md#documents)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "Every Print button prints on the range's printer if one is set up and its print agent is online; otherwise the PDF opens (see [When there is no printer](../explanation/printing.md#fallback))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "Why a print agent and how it works: [How printing works](../explanation/printing.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:9
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Setting up printers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:12
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Ranges → Set up the printers** (permission *Ranges and printers*) has three parts:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Print agents**: the computers that print for this range, each with its version and operating system, *online* or when it was last seen, and its number of printers. **Add print agent** adds a headless agent and shows its token once, **Connect by code** connects the [app](#app) by its [code](#connect), **revoke** removes an agent immediately."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Documents**: per document the printer (*browser (PDF)* keeps opening the PDF) and the options the agent reports for that printer; on Linux further `lp` options such as `fit-to-page` go in the text field. *Certificates* are the certificates from the rankings, *Print forms (pre-printed)* every other form of the club. **Save** stores the row. **Test page** prints a small page (90 × 29 mm) with club, range, printer, options and the time on the printer of that row, also before saving; it needs an online agent."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Recent jobs** shows what was printed and whether it worked."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "A job that the agent does not confirm within two minutes is retried; after three attempts it fails."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid "Step by step: [Connect a printer at the range](../how-to/connect-printer.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:23
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The Standblatt Print Agent app {#app}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "The app is the simple way for a laptop or PC next to the printers: no token and no settings to type."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "Download, install and connect it: [Connect a printer at the range](../how-to/connect-printer.md#app)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:30
#, markdown-text
msgid "![The Standblatt Print Agent app](../images/app/print-agent.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid "The window shows for each range whether it prints, with its last jobs, and below the printers of the computer, each with a **Test page** that prints on that computer without Standblatt. **Advanced** has *Start with the computer*, the address of Standblatt (change it only for a test server) and removing a range. Closing the window keeps the app running in the system tray: the icon is green when every range prints, red otherwise."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:34
#, markdown-text
msgid "On Windows and on a Mac the app tells when a new version is out; **Update now** installs it and restarts the app. To give up a computer, remove its range under **Advanced**, revoke its agent on **Ranges → Set up the printers** and uninstall the app (on Windows under *Settings → Apps*)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:35
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Connecting a computer by code {#connect}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:39
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Connect a print agent** (opened by the app with a code such as `K7QD-4MZP`) shows the computer and asks for club, range and name; only members who may manage ranges can connect a computer, and a code is valid for ten minutes. **Connect by code** on **Ranges → Set up the printers** connects it to that range under its own name. Steps: [Connect a printer at the range](../how-to/connect-printer.md#app).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:1
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:14
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Programmes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "Programmes belong to an event and are managed under **Configuration** → **Programmes** (permission *Configure events*)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![The programme list](../images/screenshots/setup.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:7
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Adding programmes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**New programme** opens an empty programme page."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Add from … → Programme library**: a template of the global library, maintained by the platform operator."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Add from … → Earlier event**: copies all programmes of another event of the club, including combinations and special prizes. Programmes whose name and variant already exist are skipped."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Add from … → Programme file**: imports a [programme file](../reference/programme-file.md) exported from another event or club."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:14
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The programme page {#page}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:17
#, markdown-text
msgid "A click on a programme in the list opens its page. It has the sections of the programme, plus a section for each switched-on [module](events.md#modules) that adds to programmes; **Create** or **Save** at the bottom saves them together."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Programme page](../images/screenshots/programme-editor.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Name** and **Variant**: programmes with the same name are variants of each other; a shooter registers for one of them. The name field suggests the names of the event's programmes, and as soon as the name matches one, the page says that you are creating a variant and warns when the variant name is empty or already taken."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Barcode**: printed on the lane sheet for electronic scoring (see [Codes](../reference/codes.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Counts for the club competition** and **Show on kiosk displays**: only while the modules *Club competition* and *Kiosk displays* are on."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Series**: shots, maximum points, whether mouches are tracked and whether **Single shots** are recorded, per series. With single shots, every shot can be entered and the series is their sum, e.g. to print them onto a form; the series total alone can still be entered."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Attempts** (module *Attempts*, see below): how often a shooter may shoot the programme at the event."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Prices (CHF)**: only the ticked age categories may shoot the programme. With several attempts, a second field per category is the price of every further attempt (*Nachdoppel*); empty means the same price, 0 means the programme is paid once."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Awards** (module *Awards*): name, kind (wreath card, prize in kind or cash prize paid out in money), value and the minimum total per age category; leave a category empty where the award is not available."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid "Once shooters are registered for a programme, the **series** are fixed (see [Why the series are locked](../explanation/rankings.md#locked)); the page says so and greys them out. Everything else can still be changed: name, variant, description, barcode, the flags, prices, series names, award names, values and limits. Age categories and awards can be **added** but not removed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "The section **Use** of a saved programme is saved at once with every change, also while shooters are registered:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Active**: inactive programmes cannot be chosen for new registrations; existing ones keep them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Combinable with**: the programme whose series this one may take at registration (not for programmes with several attempts)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Range** (events on several ranges): the range the programme is shot on, e.g. *Pistol 50 m*; the registration then offers only its lanes and kiosk displays group the rankings by range. *any* leaves it open. Programmes of different ranges need separate registrations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Print form** (when the club has [print forms](print-forms.md)): the form the results of the programme are printed onto; *none* prints no form."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:38
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Special prizes** (module *Special prizes*, see below) follow as a section of their own. **Export** at the top of the page downloads the programme as a file; **Delete** in the programme's menu in the list is only possible while nobody is registered.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:39
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Attempts {#attempts}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "By default a shooter shoots a programme once per event. **Attempts per shooter** allows more, e.g. 3 for a lucky target with further attempts at a shooting festival, or **Unlimited** for an annual programme shot over the season."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:46
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Counting attempt** decides which attempt the ranking, the club competition, special prizes and *My training* count: **The best** (by the ranking rules), **The first** or **The last**. The ranking shows it as *2/3*: the second of three attempts counts (see [Attempts and the counting attempt](../explanation/rankings.md#attempts))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:46
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Only the counting attempt receives an award**: off, every attempt can earn its award (a wreath card per further attempt); on, only the counting attempt gets one, and the award moves when a better attempt is shot."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:46
#, markdown-text
msgid "At registration, a programme with several attempts shows a counter: two attempts at once are two result cards, *Attempt 1* and *Attempt 2*. Further attempts can also be added later in a new registration, or by entering another result on **Enter results**, until the shooter has no attempts left."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:48
#, markdown-text
msgid "The number of attempts can be changed while shooters are registered, but not below the attempts a shooter already has. Programmes with several attempts cannot be combined."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:50
#, markdown-text
msgid "Step by step for a season: [Run an annual programme over the season](../how-to/annual-programme.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:54
#, markdown-text
msgid "The section **Special prizes** on the programme page awards the best ranks of every age category, for example ranks 1–3 in every category with at least 10 participants, counting only shooters whose club has at least 4 participants in this programme. Skipped shooters make room for the next one. The exact rule is in [Competition rules](../reference/rules.md#special-prizes); the winners are in the report *Special prizes* under [Statistics](statistics-reports.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:56
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Special prizes of a programme](../images/screenshots/special-prizes.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:57
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Save special prizes** stores them; ranks 0 turns special prizes off. The settings can be changed at any time until the event is closed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/ranges.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Ranges"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/ranges.md:4
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Ranges** (permission *Ranges and printers*) lists the shooting ranges of the club.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/ranges.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Ranges](../images/screenshots/ranges.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/ranges.md:11
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Name** and **Number of lanes**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/ranges.md:11
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Out of service**: lane numbers that cannot be used, e.g. `3, 7`. They show grey on the dashboard and cannot be assigned."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/ranges.md:11
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Distances**: a hall with 25 m and 50 m lanes is set up as two ranges, e.g. *Pistol 25 m* and *Pistol 50 m*, each with lanes from 1. An event can be shot on both (see [Events](events.md)), a programme can be tied to one of them (see [Programmes](programmes.md)), and one print agent can serve both (see [How printing works](../explanation/printing.md#range))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/ranges.md:11
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Set up the printers** opens the printers and print agents of the range (see [Printing](printing.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/ranges.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "To connect a printer step by step: [Connect a printer at the range](../how-to/connect-printer.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/ranges.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "A range with events cannot be deleted. Lane reservations belong to the range and show in all of its events (see [Reservations](reservations.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Rankings and kiosk"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:3
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Rankings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Rankings** shows a live ranking per programme, ordered by the [SSV rules](../reference/rules.md#ranking). The first three ranks are highlighted.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "How the programme rankings, classifications, club competition and special prizes relate: [How rankings fit together](../explanation/rankings.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Rankings](../images/screenshots/rankings.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "**PDF** opens the ranking (A4) for printing or sharing, **CSV** downloads it for Excel. Rankings do not go to the range's printer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "Programmes switched off for kiosk displays are still ranked here and marked *not on kiosk*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "[Classifications](classifications.md) follow the programmes, one table per class; their **PDF** and **CSV** are the report *Classifications*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Certificates** prints certificates for the best ranks onto a [print form](print-forms.md#certificates) of the club (see [Print certificates for the best ranks](../how-to/certificates.md)); the button appears once the club has a form that prints a rank."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:16
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Kiosk screens"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "A kiosk link shows the rankings of one event on a screen in the hall, without login; set one up with [Show the rankings on a screen in the hall](../how-to/kiosk.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Kiosk displays** in the configuration (module *Kiosk displays*) lists the links. A new one takes a name, **Dark** or **Light**, a language and, on an event with several ranges, a range; **Create kiosk link** shows the link only once.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "The kiosk shows only programmes and classifications with *Show on kiosk displays* switched on, and, with the module *Lane assignment*, the lane status if *Show lane status on the rankings* is on **Kiosk displays**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "The link sets theme, language and range (see [URL parameters](../reference/links.md#parameters))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "The **Fullscreen** button at the top right switches the screen to full screen."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "The screen updates live and reconnects by itself after a network interruption. When a new version of Standblatt is released, it reloads by itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "**revoke** in the list stops a link immediately. *last seen* tells when a screen last fetched data."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Registrations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "A registration puts a shooter on a lane with the programmes they shoot. Open it from the dashboard search (**Register for …**)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Registration dialog](../images/screenshots/registration.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:7
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Lane"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "Pick a free lane in the grid, or leave it empty: the shooter then waits until you assign a lane by editing the registration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "Occupied and out-of-service lanes cannot be picked."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "A reserved lane asks for confirmation before it is used."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:17
#, markdown-text
msgid "The programmes of the event with their price for the shooter's age category. Programmes without a price for that category are greyed out (*not for this age category*)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Variants** (same programme name) appear as a choice of one."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "A **combinable** programme offers *take N series from …*: tick it and pick exactly N series of the other programme. The other programme is added automatically if it is not chosen yet."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "The **total** at the bottom adds up the prices."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:22
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Shooter already registered"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid "If the shooter is or was registered at this event before, a notice lists those registrations with their programmes and a link to open them. Programmes already booked are locked (*already registered*, or *no attempts left* for programmes with several [attempts](programmes.md#attempts)); a shooter may still shoot another variant in a separate registration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:29
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Print lane sheet* and *Print control strip* are ticked by default (they only appear while the modules *Lane sheet* and *Control strip* are on, see [Modules](events.md#modules)): the documents print on the range's printers right after registering, or open as PDF if no printer is set up (see [Printing](printing.md)). [Print forms](print-forms.md#certificates) of the club that print a registration, e.g. a participant card, add a button each.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:30
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Editing and deleting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open a registration from the dashboard (**Edit**) or from the results (*Edit registration*) to change the lane or the programmes. Programmes that already have results cannot be removed; changing the picked series of a combination copies the new series. **Delete** removes the registration with its results after a confirmation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/reservations.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Reservations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/reservations.md:4
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Reservations** blocks lanes of the event's range for a time, for example for a training or a group. It is the page of the module *Reservations*, which needs a range and *Lane assignment*.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/reservations.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Reservations](../images/screenshots/reservations.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/reservations.md:8
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**New reservation** asks for:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/reservations.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Description** and, on several ranges, the **Range**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/reservations.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Lanes**: a list like `5` or `1, 5, 7-10`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/reservations.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**From** and **To**: the time span. Reservations on the same lane may not overlap; back-to-back is fine."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/reservations.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Show as reserved (minutes before)**: lead time from which the lanes show as reserved on the dashboard and kiosk."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/reservations.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "The list marks every reservation *planned*, *active* or *finished*; **show past** adds the finished ones. Its menu offers **Edit**, **Copy** and **Delete**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/reservations.md:17
#, markdown-text
msgid "Reservations belong to the range, so they appear in every event on that range. Reserved lanes can still be assigned to a shooter after a confirmation. The server announces the start and end of reservations by itself, so screens change without reloading."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/reservations.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "Requests that external clubs send through [online booking](online-booking.md) are listed above the reservations; once confirmed, they become ordinary reservations named after the club."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results-entry.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Enter results"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results-entry.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "Results can be entered in three ways; they can be mixed within one event:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results-entry.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "**At the lane** on a tablet or phone, through a scorer link (see [Helpers](helpers.md)): the scorer enters the series, or every shot, of the shooters on their lanes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results-entry.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "**At the desk** through the registration and its results (see [Results](results.md)), the way of a shooting festival."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results-entry.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Afterwards** on **Enter results** in the event's sidebar, shooter by shooter, e.g. from paper sheets or the display of the scoring system, or as a file exported from the scoring system. This page describes both."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results-entry.md:9
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Shooter by shooter {#quick}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results-entry.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "Choose the **Programme**; it stays chosen for the next shooters."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results-entry.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "Type a licence number or a name into **Shooter** and press ++enter++: the first hit is taken. A barcode scanner works too. **New shooter** adds someone who is not in the master data yet."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results-entry.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "Type the series, or the single shots for series that record them (see [Programmes](programmes.md)), and press ++enter++."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results-entry.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "The result is saved at once and the shooter is listed under *Entered now* with a link to the results; for a programme with a [print form](print-forms.md), the line offers **Print onto form**. If the shooter was registered at the desk for this programme and has no results yet, the results go into that registration; otherwise a registration without a lane is created, already completed. A shooter can have results in a programme only once, unless the programme allows several [attempts](programmes.md#attempts): then every further result is a new attempt until none is left."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results-entry.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "Awards are chosen as usual: the most valuable award reached is set automatically and can be changed in the results."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results-entry.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "Keys and scanners: [Keyboard and scanner](../reference/shortcuts.md#quick-entry)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results-entry.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Import from a file {#import}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results-entry.md:23
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Import CSV** (permission *Configure events*) on **Enter results** reads a file with one line per shooter and programme, e.g. exported from the scoring system or typed in a spreadsheet; the columns are described under [CSV import](../reference/csv-import.md#results). Every line is checked first; with any error nothing is imported. Step by step and how to fix line errors: [Import results from the scoring system](../how-to/import-results.md).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open the results of a registration with the **Results** button on the dashboard or by scanning the code on the lane sheet."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Results dialog](../images/screenshots/results.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:7
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Entering series"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "The cursor starts in the first empty series and moves on by itself (see [Keyboard and scanner](../reference/shortcuts.md#results))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "Series that track mouches have a second field for them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "Series with single shots show a field per shot under the series; the series becomes their sum. Enter every shot or none: without shots, the series total is typed as usual."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "++enter++ or **Save** stores the programme. Values above the maximum are marked and cannot be saved."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "Saving again replaces the results; the chosen award stays as long as the new total still reaches it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "A combined programme shows which series it takes from its source programme and fills in automatically once the source has results."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "A completed programme with a [print form](print-forms.md) shows **Print onto form**, which prints its results onto the pre-printed sheet."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "When every programme has results, the registration is completed and its lane is free again. **Print result sheet** prints an A5 summary for the shooter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:24
#, markdown-text
msgid "Once a programme is complete, the awards the total reaches in the shooter's age category are listed, the most valuable first; of several wreath cards (or several prizes in kind) only the most valuable one reached is offered. Saving the results already gives the most valuable one; picking another one saves it at once. For a wreath card, **Print wreath card** prints the shooter's data onto a pre-printed A6 card; the value is printed only if the event setting *Print the award value on wreath cards* is on (in figures and in words)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:25
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Handing out awards {#handout}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:27
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Awards handed out** in the results dialog records the handout; the registration then shows a green *awards handed out* badge, until then *awards to hand out*. **Take back** undoes it. Steps and the report of open awards: [Hand out awards and cash prizes](../how-to/hand-out-awards.md).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/shooters-clubs.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Shooters and clubs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/shooters-clubs.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "Each club keeps its own shooter master data; nothing is shared with other clubs (see [Shooter master data per club](../explanation/data.md#shooters)). **Shooters** and **Clubs** are under **Master data** in the sidebar."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/shooters-clubs.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Shooters"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/shooters-clubs.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Shooters](../images/screenshots/shooters.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/shooters-clubs.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Search** works like on the dashboard: license number (leading zeros optional), part of a name, or first and last name in either order. The list shows 50 shooters per page, the club list 50 clubs; the arrows below turn the pages."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/shooters-clubs.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "Clicking a shooter opens the details: name, license number, birthday, address and the clubs the shooter belongs to."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/shooters-clubs.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Club** (new shooter, or adding a club in the details) suggests the clubs of the list. A name that matches a club regardless of upper case and spaces is that club. Any other name shows *is not in the club list yet* with similar clubs under *Did you mean*; a new club is only created after **Create new club**, so a typo does not become a second club."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/shooters-clubs.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Import CSV** (*Manage master data*) reads a CSV file, see [CSV import](../reference/csv-import.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/shooters-clubs.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "Shooters with registrations cannot be deleted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/shooters-clubs.md:15
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Clubs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/shooters-clubs.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Clubs](../images/screenshots/clubs.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/shooters-clubs.md:20
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Clubs** are the clubs shooters belong to, with their SSV number. They appear in registrations, rankings and the club competition. A shooter can belong to several clubs and registers for one of them. Clubs used by registrations cannot be deleted, and two clubs cannot have the same name regardless of upper case and spaces. Why these are not the club that uses Standblatt: [The shooter's club and the tenant club](../explanation/data.md#shooter-club).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/shooters-clubs.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Merge into…** (*Manage master data*) cleans up a duplicate, e.g. *S.G. Hiltown* next to *SG Hilltown*: choose the club that stays (clubs with a similar name come first). It keeps its name and gets the shooters, registrations and booking requests of the other one, including those of closed events, so their rankings show the club that stays; the SSV number is taken over when it has none. The other club is deleted.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/statistics-reports.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Statistics and reports"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/statistics-reports.md:4
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Statistics** shows the key figures of the event and offers all reports.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/statistics-reports.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Statistics](../images/screenshots/statistics.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/statistics-reports.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "Registrations, completion rate, programmes sold, revenue, awards and their value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/statistics-reports.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "Participation and revenue per programme, registrations per age category, awards given."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/statistics-reports.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "The **club competition** with ranked, out-of-competition and not ranked clubs (rules: [Club competition](../reference/rules.md#club-competition))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/statistics-reports.md:11
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Reports"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/statistics-reports.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "Every report is available as **PDF** and **CSV**; which reports there are and what they contain: [Reports](../reference/documents.md#reports). Awards still to collect: [See what is still open](../how-to/hand-out-awards.md#open)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/statistics-reports.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "Below the reports, the ranking of every programme can be downloaded as PDF or CSV."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Users"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:4
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Users** lists the accounts with access to the club, the open invitations and the roles of the club. It is open to roles with the permission *Users and club*, so at least to admins.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Users](../images/screenshots/users.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:7
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Members and invitations {#invitations}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Invite by email**: paste one or many addresses (comma separated or one per line, up to 300) and choose the role. Every address gets a mail with a link valid for seven days; the list under the form says what happened to each address. Mails leave at about four per second, so a large list takes a minute."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Accepting**: the link opens a page that says which club invites with which role. Without an account the person chooses a password and is logged in at once; the email address is the login. Whoever has an account with the address logs in first and then accepts. Only then does the person appear among the members."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Invitations** below the members lists the open and the expired ones: **Send again** mails a new link (the old one stops working), **Withdraw** cancels the invitation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Add user**: for an account without email, such as a shared account at the range: an existing account is added by its user name; for a new account also enter a password (at least 10 characters)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Role**: choose the role of a member in the list. A club always keeps at least one admin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Remove** takes away the access to this club; the account itself stays and keeps its other clubs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "What a member may do depends on the role. The matrix under **Roles** has a column per role and a row per permission; a tick gives the permission at once."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Roles](../images/screenshots/roles.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid "Every permission and what it allows: [Permissions](../reference/permissions.md#permissions). Every club starts with the roles **Admin**, **Board**, **Helper** and **Member** (see [Default roles](../reference/permissions.md#default-roles))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:25
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**New role** adds a role of your own, which may only see the events until you tick more. The pencil renames a role (an empty name keeps the default name), the bin deletes it once nobody has it any more. The app shows each member only the pages and buttons their role allows: a member without *Run events* opens an event on its rankings.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid "Members with *Users and club* but without the admin role stay within their own permissions: they give, change, remove and invite only with roles whose permissions they have themselves, and make or change roles only within them. So only admins make, change or remove admins."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "Accounts are global (see [One account, a role per club](../explanation/data.md#accounts)): deleting an account is done by the platform operator in the admin panel. For a forgotten password see [Forgotten password](login-language.md#password)."
msgstr ""
